//@version=6
// =============================================================================
// MNQ ICT CONFLUENCE  --  STAGE 6 of 6: ENTRY, GUARD RAILS, ALERTS  [COMPLETE]
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// DISCLAIMER: research/education tool. NOT financial advice. Every level and
// threshold in here is an untested hypothesis about how MNQ behaves. Trade your
// own money at your own risk.
//
// Instrument : MNQ (Micro E-mini Nasdaq-100, CME)
//              tick 0.25 pts | tick value $0.50 | point value $2.00
// Chart      : 5-minute
// Plan       : TradingView PLUS. This script deliberately uses NONE of:
//              request.footprint(), seconds-based intervals, Bar Magnifier,
//              Deep Backtesting. It is an indicator, not a strategy.
//
// WHAT STAGE 1 CONTAINS
//   A. Session engine (Asia / London, trading-day attribution, shading)
//   B. ATR + rolling median of completed session ranges
//   C. Liquidity pool map (Asia range, PDH/PDL, PWH/PWL, swings, EQH/EQL)
//   D. Anti-repaint fractal swing pivots
//   E. Debug verification table
//   F. Empty, clearly-marked stubs for stages 3-6
//
// WHAT STAGE 2 ADDS
//   G. Displacement bars (expansion candles with real bodies)
//   H. Liquidity sweep detection as an explicit per-pool state machine
//      (PENETRATED -> SWEPT | BROKEN OUT | EXPIRED), plus a Sweep record book
//   I. BOS / CHoCH / MSS from confirmed pivots only, and the sweep+MSS pairing
//      that stage 5 will score
//   J. Stage-2 visuals, bounded
//
// WHAT STAGE 3 ADDS
//   K. Zone types + the shared state enum
//   L. Fair value gaps, and inverse FVGs when one fails on a close through
//   M. Displacement-anchored order blocks, and breakers when one fails
//   N. Dealing range from a sweep+MSS pair -> premium / discount / OTE
//   O. THE UNIFIED POI API. Order blocks and FVGs are collinear evidence: the
//      same displacement leg usually produces both at the same coordinates.
//      Stage 5 must therefore query ONE component, not two, or it will pay
//      itself twice for a single observation. bestPOI() is that one query;
//      the underlying kind is retained for diagnostics only.
//   P. Stage-3 visuals, bounded
//
// WHAT STAGE 4 ADDS
//   Q. SMT divergence against a correlated reference (ES). CONFLUENCE ONLY --
//      it can never arm a setup by itself, and stage 5 weights it at 1 point.
//
// WHAT STAGE 5 ADDS
//   R. The six-component confluence score, its mandatory gate, the per-setup
//      score distribution, and a full breakdown of every component so a score
//      can always be explained rather than merely reported.
//
// WHAT STAGE 6 ADDS
//   S. The entry trigger, the structural stop, the two-target plan, position
//      sizing, every guard rail with its own counter, and alert() calls.
//      This is an INDICATOR: nothing here places an order. The "position" it
//      tracks is virtual, and exists so TP1/stop/runner alerts can fire.
//
// ANTI-REPAINT CONTRACT (holds for every stage of this project)
//   1. Session membership comes from the bar's OPEN time, which is fixed the
//      moment the bar prints, so session flags can never repaint.
//   2. Every state mutation a future signal could depend on lives inside an
//      `if barstate.isconfirmed` block. Nothing is written from a forming bar.
//   3. Every request.security() uses lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off AND a
//      [1] offset on the requested expression, so we only ever read a period
//      that has already CLOSED.
//   4. Swing pivots are registered pivotLen bars late, by construction. The lag
//      is real and is never papered over.
//   6. Pools carry a TIER. The drawing-object cap evicts transient pools first
//      and never evicts a protected one, so the day/week/session levels cannot
//      be pushed out of the book by a burst of swings.
//   5. All clock logic uses the "America/New_York" string, so US DST shifts are
//      handled by TradingView. No hardcoded UTC offsets anywhere.
// =============================================================================

// max_bars_back is raised because stage 3 reads close[k]/open[k] with a SERIES
// offset when it hunts backwards for an order-block anchor candle. Pine cannot
// infer the required buffer from a variable offset, so we state it.
indicator("MNQ ICT Confluence [S6]", shorttitle = "MNQ ICT", overlay = true,
     max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_boxes_count = 500,
     max_bars_back = 500)

// =============================================================================
// INPUTS
// =============================================================================

// ---- Group: Sessions ---------------------------------------------------------
grpSess = "Sessions"

asiaEnabled = input.bool(true, "Asia enabled", group = grpSess,
     tooltip = "Turns Asia session flags and shading on/off. The Asia RANGE is tracked either way so pools stay correct.")
asiaSession = input.session("2000-0200", "Asia session (ET)", group = grpSess,
     tooltip = "Spans midnight. This full window always builds the Asia range high/low.")
asiaExcludeLate = input.bool(true, "Exclude late Asia 00:00-02:00 from signals", group = grpSess,
     tooltip = "When on, the 00:00-02:00 ET tail is suppressed for SIGNAL purposes only. It is STILL used to build the Asia range high/low.")

londonEnabled = input.bool(true, "London enabled", group = grpSess)
londonPreset  = input.string("Killzone 02:00-05:00", "London preset", group = grpSess,
     options = ["Killzone 02:00-05:00", "Extended 02:00-06:00", "Legacy 03:00-07:00"])
londonUseCustom = input.bool(false, "Override preset with custom London window", group = grpSess,
     tooltip = "Switch on to ignore the preset and use the custom session string below.")
londonSessionCustom = input.session("0200-0500", "London session custom (ET)", group = grpSess,
     tooltip = "Only used when the override above is on.")

// ---- Group: Structure --------------------------------------------------------
grpStruct = "Structure"

pivotLen = input.int(2, "Pivot length (bars each side)", minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = grpStruct,
     tooltip = "Fractal confirmation. A pivot is only KNOWN pivotLen bars after it prints.")
atrLen = input.int(14, "ATR length", minval = 1, group = grpStruct)

// -- stage 2 additions to the Structure group --
requireDisplacementForMSS = input.bool(true, "MSS requires displacement in the breaking leg", group = grpStruct,
     tooltip = "When off, MSS is identical to CHoCH. When on, a CHoCH is only promoted to MSS if the leg from the broken swing to the break contains a displacement bar in the same direction.")
mssMaxBarsAfterSweep = input.int(10, "Max bars from sweep to MSS", minval = 1, maxval = 100, group = grpStruct,
     tooltip = "An MSS further than this from the sweep confirmation is treated as unrelated and does not arm the pair.")

// ---- Group: Liquidity Pools --------------------------------------------------
grpPools = "Liquidity Pools"

showAsiaRange   = input.bool(true, "Draw Asia range high/low", group = grpPools)
showPDHL        = input.bool(true, "Draw prior day high/low",  group = grpPools)
showPWHL        = input.bool(true, "Draw prior week high/low", group = grpPools)
showEqualLevels = input.bool(true, "Draw equal highs/lows",    group = grpPools)

equalTolTicks = input.float(3.0, "Equal-level tolerance (ticks)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.25, group = grpPools,
     tooltip = "MNQ tick = 0.25 pts, so 3 ticks = 0.75 pts.")
equalTolAtrMult = input.float(0.10, "Equal-level tolerance (x ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.01, group = grpPools)
equalTolMode = input.string("Max of both", "Equal-level tolerance mode", group = grpPools,
     options = ["Ticks", "ATR", "Max of both"])

pdhlSource = input.string("RTH 09:30-16:00", "Prior day high/low source", group = grpPools,
     options = ["RTH 09:30-16:00", "Full session"],
     tooltip = "RTH builds the level natively from intraday bars. Full session reads the prior CLOSED daily bar.")

maxPools = input.int(56, "Max pools kept (drawings capped)", minval = 5, maxval = 200, group = grpPools,
     tooltip = "Hard cap on stored pools and their line/label objects. Transient (swing) pools are evicted first; protected levels never are.")
maxEqualPools = input.int(8, "Max EQH / EQL pools (each side)", minval = 1, maxval = 50, group = grpPools,
     tooltip = "Per-tag cap on equal-high and equal-low clusters. Without this the EQ pools grow without bound and saturate the book.")

// ---- Group: Displacement -----------------------------------------------------
grpDisplace = "Displacement"

dispMode = input.string("Either", "Displacement size test", group = grpDisplace,
     options = ["ATR multiple", "Median range multiple", "Either"],
     tooltip = "ATR adapts slowly; the median of recent bar ranges adapts fast. Either = the bar qualifies if it clears one of them.")
dispAtrMult    = input.float(1.5, "Displacement x ATR", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = grpDisplace)
dispMedianMult = input.float(1.5, "Displacement x median bar range", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = grpDisplace)
dispMedianLen  = input.int(20, "Median bar-range lookback", minval = 2, maxval = 200, group = grpDisplace,
     tooltip = "Bars used for the rolling median of bar range. The CURRENT bar is excluded from its own median.")
dispRequireBodyPct = input.float(0.5, "Min body as fraction of bar range", minval = 0.0, maxval = 1.0, step = 0.05, group = grpDisplace,
     tooltip = "Rejects huge-wick dojis. 0.5 means the body must be at least half the bar's total range.")

// ---- Group: Sweeps -----------------------------------------------------------
grpSweep = "Sweeps"

sweepMinTier = input.string("Protected + Equal", "Sweep target significance", group = grpSweep,
     options = ["Protected only", "Protected + Equal", "All including swings"],
     tooltip = "Swing-only sweeps are noise on a 5m chart. Opt in deliberately.")
sweepPenTicks   = input.float(2.0, "Penetration (ticks)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.25, group = grpSweep,
     tooltip = "MNQ tick = 0.25 pts, so 2 ticks = 0.5 pts. Price must clear the pool by at least this before it counts as penetrated.")
sweepPenAtrMult = input.float(0.05, "Penetration (x ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.01, group = grpSweep)
sweepPenMode    = input.string("Max of both", "Penetration mode", group = grpSweep,
     options = ["Ticks", "ATR", "Max of both"])
sweepReclaimBars = input.int(1, "Bars allowed to reclaim", minval = 0, maxval = 20, group = grpSweep,
     tooltip = "After penetration, price has this many FURTHER bars to close back on the correct side. The penetration bar itself always counts, so a single rejection wick confirms immediately.")
breakoutClosesToInvalidate = input.int(2, "Consecutive closes beyond = breakout", minval = 1, maxval = 10, group = grpSweep,
     tooltip = "This many consecutive closes beyond the pool means the level failed. The pool is consumed and no sweep is recorded.")
sweepValidBars = input.int(12, "Sweep stays live for N bars", minval = 1, maxval = 200, group = grpSweep,
     tooltip = "How long a confirmed sweep remains available to pair with an MSS.")
carryPriorAsiaRange = input.bool(true, "Carry prior Asia range into the Asia session", group = grpSweep,
     tooltip = "Re-states the previous session's Asia high/low as fresh active pools tagged Prior Asia High/Low, so Asia has targets before its own range is finalised.")

// ---- Group: FVG --------------------------------------------------------------
grpFvg = "FVG"

fvgMinTicks   = input.float(4.0, "Min gap (ticks)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.25, group = grpFvg,
     tooltip = "MNQ tick = 0.25 pts, so 4 ticks = 1.0 pt.")
fvgMinAtrMult = input.float(0.25, "Min gap (x ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.01, group = grpFvg)
fvgMinMode    = input.string("Max of both", "Min gap mode", group = grpFvg,
     options = ["Ticks", "ATR", "Max of both"])
fvgRequireDisplacement = input.bool(true, "Middle candle must be displacement", group = grpFvg,
     tooltip = "Uses stage 2's isDisplacementUp/Down on the middle candle of the three. A gap left by three ordinary candles is a printing artefact, not an imbalance.")
fvgMaxAgeBars   = input.int(60, "FVG max age (bars)", minval = 1, maxval = 1000, group = grpFvg)
fvgInvalidateOn = input.string("Full fill", "FVG invalidated on", group = grpFvg,
     options = ["Full fill", "CE breach", "Close through"],
     tooltip = "Full fill = price traded through the far edge. CE breach = price reached the midpoint. Close through = a body close beyond the far edge.")

ifvgRequireCloseThrough = input.bool(true, "IFVG needs a body close through", group = grpFvg,
     tooltip = "When on, an FVG only flips to an inverse FVG after a CLOSE beyond its far edge. When off, a wick through is enough.")
ifvgMaxAgeBars = input.int(40, "IFVG max age (bars)", minval = 1, maxval = 1000, group = grpFvg)

// ---- Group: Order Blocks -----------------------------------------------------
grpOb = "Order Blocks"

obLookbackForAnchor = input.int(10, "Max bars back to find anchor candle", minval = 1, maxval = 50, group = grpOb,
     tooltip = "From the structure-break bar, how far back to hunt for the last opposing candle.")
obUseWholeCandle = input.bool(false, "Use whole candle instead of body", group = grpOb,
     tooltip = "Off = body only (open to close), the stricter reading. On = full high/low range.")
obMaxAgeBars = input.int(80, "OB max age (bars)", minval = 1, maxval = 1000, group = grpOb)
obInvalidateOnCloseThrough = input.bool(true, "Close through retires the OB (becomes a breaker)", group = grpOb,
     tooltip = "When on, a body close beyond the far edge flips the block to a BREAKER with inverted polarity. When off, only age retires it.")

// ---- Group: OTE --------------------------------------------------------------
grpOte = "OTE"

oteLow  = input.float(0.62, "OTE band start (retracement)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 1.0, step = 0.01, group = grpOte)
oteHigh = input.float(0.79, "OTE band end (retracement)",   minval = 0.0, maxval = 1.0, step = 0.01, group = grpOte)
oteRequireCorrectSide = input.bool(true, "Longs only in discount, shorts only in premium", group = grpOte)
drMaxAgeBars = input.int(120, "Dealing range max age (bars)", minval = 1, maxval = 2000, group = grpOte,
     tooltip = "A dealing range with no lifetime would keep an OTE band alive forever. 120 bars is about 10 hours on a 5m chart.")

poiOverlapTolTicks = input.float(4.0, "FVG / OB coincidence tolerance (ticks)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.25, group = grpOte,
     tooltip = "How close an FVG and an order block must sit before they count as the same point of interest.")

// ---- Group: SMT --------------------------------------------------------------
grpSmt = "SMT"

smtEnabled = input.bool(true, "SMT enabled", group = grpSmt)
smtSymbol  = input.string("CME_MINI:ES1!", "Correlated reference symbol", group = grpSmt,
     tooltip = "ES is the natural pair for NQ: same exchange, same session, different index. The request uses ignore_invalid_symbol, so a typo degrades to no signal rather than a script error.")
smtLookbackBars = input.int(20, "Swing comparison window (bars)", minval = 2, maxval = 200, group = grpSmt,
     tooltip = "How far apart two confirmed pivots may sit and still be compared. Also how long a detected divergence stays live.")
smtRequireAtPool = input.bool(true, "Only count divergence at a liquidity pool", group = grpSmt,
     tooltip = "Divergence in open space is noise. At a mapped pool it is a statement about who is defending that level.")
smtPoolProxTicks = input.float(12.0, "Pool proximity (ticks)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.25, group = grpSmt,
     tooltip = "MNQ tick = 0.25 pts, so 12 ticks = 3.0 pts.")
smtMinTier = input.string("Protected + Equal", "Pool significance for the SMT gate", group = grpSmt,
     options = ["Protected only", "Protected + Equal", "All including swings"],
     tooltip = "MUST NOT be set to 'All including swings'. Stage 1 registers every confirmed pivot as a TIER_TRANSIENT pool at exactly that pivot's price, on the same confirmed bar the SMT test then runs. Including tier 2 therefore matches the pivot against a pool derived from itself at a distance of exactly zero, and the gate can never fail. Kept as a SEPARATE input from sweepMinTier so opening sweeps to swings cannot silently re-break this.")

// ---- Group: Scoring ----------------------------------------------------------
grpScore = "Scoring"

scoreThreshold  = input.float(7.0, "Signal threshold", minval = 0.0, maxval = 10.0, step = 0.1, group = grpScore,
     tooltip = "A setup fires at or above this. Chosen so that the mandatory components plus the POI component cannot reach it alone: 3.0 + 2.0 + 1.5 = 6.5, so confluence is always load-bearing.")
scoreStrongBand = input.float(8.0, "Strong band", minval = 0.0, maxval = 10.0, step = 0.1, group = grpScore,
     tooltip = "Set at 8.0 rather than 8.5 because the Asia ceiling is 9.5, not 10: SMT is halved overnight. 8.5 would sit within a point of the Asia ceiling and be effectively unreachable there.")

rangeRef = input.string("Current session", "Session P/D reference range", group = grpScore,
     options = ["Current session", "Prior day RTH", "Prior day full"],
     tooltip = "DELIBERATELY a different range from the dealing range, so this component is not collinear with the dealing-range location component. Price can sit in dealing-range discount while in session premium; those are two facts, not one.")
sessionPdDepth = input.float(0.25, "Deep premium / discount threshold", minval = 0.01, maxval = 0.5, step = 0.01, group = grpScore,
     tooltip = "0.25 means the bottom quartile of the reference range counts as deep discount for a long, the top quartile as deep premium for a short.")

// Every weight is an input so the model can be re-weighted without touching code.
wSweep     = input.float(3.0, "Weight: sweep (x poolWeight)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 10.0, step = 0.1, group = grpScore)
wMss       = input.float(2.0, "Weight: MSS confirming the sweep", minval = 0.0, maxval = 10.0, step = 0.1, group = grpScore)
wPoi       = input.float(1.5, "Weight: POI (x quality)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 10.0, step = 0.1, group = grpScore)
wLocation  = input.float(1.5, "Weight: dealing-range location", minval = 0.0, maxval = 10.0, step = 0.1, group = grpScore)
wSmt       = input.float(1.0, "Weight: SMT (x strength x session)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 10.0, step = 0.1, group = grpScore)
wSessionPd = input.float(1.0, "Weight: session premium / discount", minval = 0.0, maxval = 10.0, step = 0.1, group = grpScore)

// ---- Group: Entry ------------------------------------------------------------
grpEntry = "Entry"

entryMode = input.string("Retest limit", "Entry trigger", group = grpEntry,
     options = ["Retest limit", "MSS close", "Either"],
     tooltip = "Retest limit waits for price to trade back into the bestPOI zone between its CE and far edge. MSS close takes the close of the MSS confirmation bar. Either prefers the retest and falls back to a market entry when the retest window expires -- see the note in section S on why the fallback cannot be the MSS bar's own price.")
entryRetestBars = input.int(5, "Retest window (bars)", minval = 1, maxval = 100, group = grpEntry)
entryRequireScoreAtTrigger = input.bool(true, "Score must still pass on the trigger bar", group = grpEntry,
     tooltip = "A score that passed three bars ago and has since decayed must not fire. The score AT the trigger is recorded separately from the setup's peak; they are different numbers.")

// ---- Group: Stop -------------------------------------------------------------
grpStop = "Stop"

stopMode = input.string("Wider of the two", "Stop anchor", group = grpStop,
     options = ["Beyond swept extreme", "Beyond POI far edge", "Wider of the two"])
stopBufferTicks   = input.float(2.0, "Stop buffer (ticks)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.25, group = grpStop)
stopBufferAtrMult = input.float(0.10, "Stop buffer (x ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.01, group = grpStop)
stopBufferMode    = input.string("Max of both", "Stop buffer mode", group = grpStop,
     options = ["Ticks", "ATR", "Max of both"])
stopMinPts = input.float(8.0,  "Min structural stop (pts)", minval = 0.25, step = 0.25, group = grpStop)
stopMaxPts = input.float(30.0, "Max structural stop (pts)", minval = 0.25, step = 0.25, group = grpStop,
     tooltip = "Outside this band the signal is SUPPRESSED, never clamped. A 45-point structural stop is the structure telling us it is not what we think it is; clamping would hide that and quietly change the trade.")

// ---- Group: Targets ----------------------------------------------------------
grpTgt = "Targets"

tp1R   = input.float(1.0, "TP1 at R multiple", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = grpTgt)
tp1Pct = input.float(50.0, "Percent taken at TP1", minval = 1.0, maxval = 100.0, step = 5.0, group = grpTgt)
moveToBeAfterTp1 = input.bool(true, "Move stop to break-even after TP1", group = grpTgt)
runnerTarget = input.string("Next opposing pool", "Runner target", group = grpTgt,
     options = ["Next opposing pool", "Fixed R multiple", "Either whichever first"])
runnerFixedR = input.float(2.0, "Runner fixed R multiple", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = grpTgt)

// ---- Group: Guard Rails ------------------------------------------------------
grpGuard = "Guard Rails"

minBarsBetweenSameDir = input.int(18, "Min bars between same-direction signals", minval = 0, maxval = 500, group = grpGuard,
     tooltip = "Secondary guard. The PRIMARY debounce is the spent flag on the Sweep object: a sweep that produced a trigger can never produce another. This one catches a genuinely new sweep armed by a stale reversal leg.")
maxSignalsPerSession = input.int(2, "Max signals per session, per direction", minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = grpGuard)
exhaustMult = input.float(1.5, "Exhaustion: session range x median", minval = 0.5, step = 0.1, group = grpGuard,
     tooltip = "No entry once the session has already travelled more than this multiple of its own 20-session median range. Skipped when the median is na.")
ambiguityMargin = input.float(0.75, "Ambiguity margin", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = grpGuard,
     tooltip = "If both sides pass and their scores are within this, take NEITHER. Two opposing setups scoring the same is the model being confused, not two opportunities.")

asiaCutoff    = input.session("0145-0200", "Asia no-new-entries window (ET)", group = grpGuard,
     tooltip = "Expressed as a WINDOW running from the cutoff time to the session end, because that is the DST-safe way to say 'from this time onward' in Pine. If you change the session preset, change this to end where that session ends.")
asiaFlatten   = input.session("0155-0200", "Asia flatten window (ET)", group = grpGuard)
londonCutoff  = input.session("0445-0500", "London no-new-entries window (ET)", group = grpGuard,
     tooltip = "Sized for the default Killzone 02:00-05:00 preset. Switching London to Extended or Legacy REQUIRES changing this to match, or entries resume after 05:00.")
londonFlatten = input.session("0455-0500", "London flatten window (ET)", group = grpGuard)

// ---- Group: Risk -------------------------------------------------------------
grpRisk = "Risk"

riskUSD = input.float(200.0, "Risk per trade (USD)", minval = 1.0, step = 10.0, group = grpRisk,
     tooltip = "MNQ point value is fixed at $2.00 in code, not exposed, because changing it silently would make every size and every dollar figure wrong.")

// ---- Group: Alerts -----------------------------------------------------------
grpAlert = "Alerts"

alertPrefix = input.string("MNQ-ICT", "Alert prefix", group = grpAlert,
     tooltip = "Tags every alert() message so multiple charts can be routed apart.")

// ---- Group: Display ----------------------------------------------------------
grpDisp = "Display"

showDebugTable     = input.bool(true, "Show debug table",      group = grpDisp)
showSessionShading = input.bool(true, "Show session shading",  group = grpDisp)
showSwingMarkers   = input.bool(true, "Show confirmed swing markers", group = grpDisp,
     tooltip = "Triangles are drawn back at the TRUE pivot bar, but only appear pivotLen bars later. That visible lag IS the anti-repaint guarantee.")

// -- stage 2 additions to the Display group --
showDisplacement    = input.bool(true, "Highlight displacement bars", group = grpDisp)
showSweepMarkers    = input.bool(true, "Show sweep markers",          group = grpDisp)
showStructureLabels = input.bool(true, "Show BOS / CHoCH / MSS labels", group = grpDisp)

// -- stage 3 additions to the Display group --
showFVG  = input.bool(true, "Show fair value gaps",  group = grpDisp)
showIFVG = input.bool(true, "Show inverse FVGs",     group = grpDisp)
showOB   = input.bool(true, "Show order blocks",     group = grpDisp)
showOTE  = input.bool(true, "Show OTE band",         group = grpDisp)
fadeInvalidated = input.bool(true, "Fade invalidated zones instead of deleting", group = grpDisp,
     tooltip = "Same reasoning as retired liquidity pools: where a zone failed is information.")
showSMT = input.bool(true, "Show SMT markers", group = grpDisp)
showSignals = input.bool(true, "Show entry / stop / target lines", group = grpDisp)
compactTable = input.bool(true, "Compact table (diagnostics only)", group = grpDisp,
     tooltip = "The full table is 54 rows and runs off the bottom of most screens, which hides the score histogram -- the single most important diagnostic in the build. Compact mode shows only what you need to judge whether the model is discriminating.")
showHistoricalOTE = input.bool(false, "Keep dead OTE bands (validation mode)", group = grpDisp,
     tooltip = "Off is correct for live trading: a dealing range is a claim about right now. On is for scrolling back to audit whether the dealing-range logic was right on past setups.")

// =============================================================================
// CONSTANTS
// =============================================================================

// One timezone string for the whole script. DST handled by TradingView.
string TZ = "America/New_York"

// Fixed helper windows (deliberately not user-tunable).
string SESS_ASIA_LATE = "0000-0200"   // the Asia tail we can mute for signals
string SESS_RTH       = "0930-1600"   // US cash session, for RTH PDH/PDL

// How many completed session ranges feed the rolling median.
int MEDIAN_LOOKBACK = 20

// How many recent confirmed swings we keep in memory (and as pools).
int SWING_KEEP = 10

// CME futures roll the trading day at 18:00 ET. Any bar at or after this hour
// belongs to the NEXT calendar trading day. This is what makes a Sunday 20:00
// ET Asia open belong to Monday.
int TRADING_DAY_ROLL_HOUR = 18

// Pool TIERS. Lower number = more significant = harder to evict.
//   0 protected   : session / day / week levels. Never evicted by the cap.
//   1 significant : equal highs and lows (clustered, so deliberate).
//   2 transient   : individual swing pivots. First to go under pressure.
int TIER_PROTECTED   = 0
int TIER_SIGNIFICANT = 1
int TIER_TRANSIENT   = 2

// Pool colours: buy-side liquidity sits ABOVE price (red), sell-side BELOW (teal).
color colBuySide  = #ef5350
color colSellSide = #26a69a

// Stage-2 colours. Displacement gets its own hue pair so it is never confused
// with an ordinary green/red candle; structure events are ranked by how much
// they matter -- BOS is the least interesting, MSS is the one we trade around.
color colDispUp   = #00c853   // bright green expansion candle
color colDispDown = #d50000   // bright red expansion candle
color colBOS      = #90a4ae   // blue-grey: continuation, informational
color colCHoCH    = #ffa726   // amber: reversal warning
color colMSS      = #ab47bc   // purple: the structural shift that counts

// Zone STATE enum, shared by FVGs, inverse FVGs and order blocks. Plain ints
// rather than a Pine enum so the ordering is usable: any state <= ST_CE_TAGGED
// means the zone is still live, and state only ever moves forward.
//   FRESH       untouched since creation
//   TOUCHED     price has tagged the near edge
//   CE_TAGGED   price has reached the midpoint. For a POI this counts as
//               mitigated: you do not enter at a level price already visited.
//   INVALIDATED the zone failed on its configured invalidation test
//   EXPIRED     aged out without being invalidated
//   BREAKER     ORDER BLOCKS ONLY. Price closed through, so the block is dead
//               in its original polarity and live in the inverted one.
int ST_FRESH       = 0
int ST_TOUCHED     = 1
int ST_CE_TAGGED   = 2
int ST_INVALIDATED = 3
int ST_EXPIRED     = 4
int ST_BREAKER     = 5

// Stage-3 zone colours.
color colFvgBull  = #26a69a
color colFvgBear  = #ef5350
color colIfvgBull = #4dd0e1   // cyan-ish: an inverse FVG is a different animal
color colIfvgBear = #f06292
color colObBull   = #66bb6a
color colObBear   = #e57373
color colBreaker  = #ffb300   // amber, matching the CHoCH "something flipped" idea
color colOte      = #ab47bc   // same purple as MSS: the OTE band belongs to it
color colSmt      = #3949ab   // indigo, deliberately unlike the sweep cross
color colDead     = #9e9e9e   // faded, invalidated or expired

// Stage-3 object budgets. FVG/IFVG/OB boxes plus the single OTE box stay well
// inside max_boxes_count = 500.
int MAX_FVGS  = 40
int MAX_IFVGS = 20
int MAX_OBS   = 20

// MNQ point value. FIXED, deliberately not an input: every contract count and
// every dollar figure in the alerts is derived from it, so a silent change
// would make all of them wrong at once.
float MNQ_POINT_VALUE = 2.00

// Stage-6 drawing budget: four lines per signal.
int MAX_SIG_LINES = 40

// A session range smaller than one average bar is not a range. Early in a
// session a couple of ticks would flip the premium/discount reading from one
// extreme to the other, so below this floor that component abstains.
float SESS_PD_MIN_RANGE_ATR = 1.0

// SMT is halved during Asia. ES overnight books are thin enough that a 3-point
// NQ divergence maps to well under a point on ES -- inside the noise. See the
// note at the SMT component.
float SMT_ASIA_SCALE = 0.5

// How many dead dealing-range bands to keep when showHistoricalOTE is on.
// Each band costs one box plus three level lines.
int MAX_OTE_HIST = 12

// How many bars after the MSS bar a zone may still be credited to the MSS
// displacement leg. An FVG completes on its THIRD candle, so a gap left by the
// breaking bar itself is only recorded one or two bars later.
int MSS_LEG_GRACE_BARS = 2

// Stage-2 drawing budget. Labels are recycled oldest-first so the script can
// never approach the 500-object ceiling.
int MAX_S2_LABELS = 60
int MAX_SWEEPS    = 20

// =============================================================================
// SECTION B (part 1): ATR + TOLERANCE
// Chart-timeframe ATR. It is only READ inside confirmed-bar blocks, where its
// value for the bar is already final.
// =============================================================================

float atr = ta.atr(atrLen)

// Resolve the equal-highs/lows tolerance into PRICE units from the chosen mode.
f_equalTol() =>
    float tTicks = equalTolTicks * syminfo.mintick
    float tAtr   = equalTolAtrMult * nz(atr)
    float res    = switch equalTolMode
        "Ticks" => tTicks
        "ATR"   => tAtr
        => math.max(tTicks, tAtr)
    res

// =============================================================================
// SECTION C (part 1): LIQUIDITY POOL TYPE + API
// A "pool" is a resting-liquidity price level. Stages 2-6 will sweep, score and
// target these, so the API is defined now and kept deliberately small.
// =============================================================================

// price   : the level itself
// tag     : the pool's label, e.g. "Asia High", "PDH", "EQH"
// buySide : true  = buy-side liquidity  (above price: stops of shorts)
//           false = sell-side liquidity (below price: stops of longs)
// barIdx  : bar_index at which the pool was CONFIRMED. For swings this is
//           pivotLen bars AFTER the pivot itself -- that is intentional.
// tier    : 0 protected / 1 significant / 2 transient. Drives eviction order
//           under the global cap AND how stage 2 filters sweep targets.
// active  : true until a later stage marks it consumed/swept
// ln / lb : its drawing objects, carried on the object so cleanup is trivial
type Pool
    float  price
    string tag
    bool   buySide
    int    barIdx
    int    tier
    bool   active
    line   ln = na
    label  lb = na

// The single global pool book. Stages 2-6 read from this array.
var array<Pool> pools = array.new<Pool>()

// --- internal: destroy a pool's drawings and drop it from the book -----------
f_deletePoolAt(int idx) =>
    Pool p = array.get(pools, idx)
    if not na(p.ln)
        line.delete(p.ln)
    if not na(p.lb)
        label.delete(p.lb)
    array.remove(pools, idx)

// --- internal: index of the OLDEST pool in tier `t`, or -1 -------------------
// Pools are appended in time order, so the first match found IS the oldest.
f_findOldestOfTier(int t) =>
    int idx = -1
    if array.size(pools) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(pools) - 1
            if idx < 0 and array.get(pools, i).tier == t
                idx := i
    idx

// --- internal: enforce the global object cap, LEAST significant first --------
// Evicts the oldest transient pool; only if none remain, the oldest significant
// one; and never a protected one. If the book is somehow all protected we stop
// rather than evict -- protected pools are singletons and self-limiting, so the
// book cannot actually run away on them.
f_enforcePoolCap() =>
    bool stop = false
    while array.size(pools) > maxPools and not stop
        int victim = f_findOldestOfTier(TIER_TRANSIENT)
        if victim < 0
            victim := f_findOldestOfTier(TIER_SIGNIFICANT)
        if victim < 0
            stop := true
        if victim >= 0
            f_deletePoolAt(victim)

// --- internal: keep at most keepN pools carrying `tag`, dropping oldest -----
// Stops a stream of fresh swing pools from evicting the day/week levels.
f_trimTag(string tag, int keepN) =>
    int cnt = 0
    if array.size(pools) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(pools) - 1
            if array.get(pools, i).tag == tag
                cnt += 1
    int toDrop = cnt - keepN
    int cur = 0
    while toDrop > 0 and cur < array.size(pools)
        if array.get(pools, cur).tag == tag
            f_deletePoolAt(cur)
            toDrop -= 1
        else
            cur += 1

// --- PUBLIC: remove every pool carrying `tag` -------------------------------
// Used for singleton levels that get RE-STATED each day/week/session.
removePoolsByTag(string tag) =>
    if array.size(pools) > 0
        for i = array.size(pools) - 1 to 0
            if array.get(pools, i).tag == tag
                f_deletePoolAt(i)

// --- internal: map a known tag to its tier ----------------------------------
// One source of truth, so the public addPool() cannot mis-tier a level.
f_tierForTag(string tag) =>
    int t = switch tag
        "Asia High"       => TIER_PROTECTED
        "Asia Low"        => TIER_PROTECTED
        "Prior Asia High" => TIER_PROTECTED
        "Prior Asia Low"  => TIER_PROTECTED
        "PDH"       => TIER_PROTECTED
        "PDL"       => TIER_PROTECTED
        "PWH"       => TIER_PROTECTED
        "PWL"       => TIER_PROTECTED
        "EQH"       => TIER_SIGNIFICANT
        "EQL"       => TIER_SIGNIFICANT
        => TIER_TRANSIENT
    t

// --- internal: the full add, with explicit tier and "should this be drawn" --
f_addPool(float price, string tag, bool buySide, int tier, bool draw) =>
    Pool p = Pool.new(price = price, tag = tag, buySide = buySide,
                     barIdx = bar_index, tier = tier, active = true)
    if draw
        color c = buySide ? colBuySide : colSellSide
        p.ln := line.new(bar_index, price, bar_index + 1, price,
                 xloc = xloc.bar_index, extend = extend.right,
                 color = color.new(c, 35), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
        p.lb := label.new(bar_index + 3, price, tag,
                 xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left,
                 color = color.new(color.black, 100), textcolor = color.new(c, 10),
                 size = size.small)
    array.push(pools, p)
    f_enforcePoolCap()
    p

// --- PUBLIC: addPool(price, label, side) ------------------------------------
// The stage-2+ entry point. Adds a drawn pool and returns it. The tier is
// derived from the tag, so callers cannot forget to set it.
addPool(float price, string tag, bool buySide) =>
    f_addPool(price, tag, buySide, f_tierForTag(tag), true)

// --- PUBLIC: move an existing pool's price (and its drawings) ---------------
setPoolPrice(Pool p, float price) =>
    p.price := price
    if not na(p.ln)
        line.set_y1(p.ln, price)
        line.set_y2(p.ln, price)
    if not na(p.lb)
        label.set_y(p.lb, price)

// --- PUBLIC: nearest ACTIVE buy-side pool ABOVE px, tier-filtered -----------
// maxTier = 0 -> protected levels only (Asia/PD/PW)
// maxTier = 1 -> also equal highs
// maxTier = 2 -> also individual swing highs
// Stage 2 should sweep against a TIGHT tier, so a 20-minute-old swing high is
// not treated as equal in weight to the Asia session high.
nearestBuySideAboveTier(float px, int maxTier) =>
    Pool best = na
    if array.size(pools) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(pools) - 1
            Pool p = array.get(pools, i)
            if p.active and p.buySide and p.tier <= maxTier and p.price > px
                if na(best)
                    best := p
                else if p.price < best.price
                    best := p
    best

// --- PUBLIC: nearest ACTIVE sell-side pool BELOW px, tier-filtered ----------
nearestSellSideBelowTier(float px, int maxTier) =>
    Pool best = na
    if array.size(pools) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(pools) - 1
            Pool p = array.get(pools, i)
            if p.active and not p.buySide and p.tier <= maxTier and p.price < px
                if na(best)
                    best := p
                else if p.price > best.price
                    best := p
    best

// --- PUBLIC: nearest ACTIVE buy-side pool strictly ABOVE px -----------------
// Unfiltered form, kept so existing callers are unaffected. Pine forbids
// default arguments on user functions, so this delegates instead.
nearestBuySideAbove(float px) =>
    nearestBuySideAboveTier(px, TIER_TRANSIENT)

// --- PUBLIC: nearest ACTIVE sell-side pool strictly BELOW px ----------------
nearestSellSideBelow(float px) =>
    nearestSellSideBelowTier(px, TIER_TRANSIENT)

// --- PUBLIC: significance weight for a tier ---------------------------------
// STAGE 5 will multiply the sweep component's score contribution by this, so
// taking out the Asia high counts fully while running a single swing pivot
// contributes only a fraction. NOT USED YET -- declared here so the scale is
// fixed in one place before scoring is written.
poolWeight(int tier) =>
    float w = switch tier
        0 => 1.0
        1 => 0.6
        => 0.3
    w

// --- PUBLIC: first ACTIVE pool with `tag` within `tol` of price, else na ----
findActivePoolNear(string tag, float price, float tol) =>
    Pool hit = na
    if array.size(pools) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(pools) - 1
            Pool p = array.get(pools, i)
            if p.active and p.tag == tag and math.abs(p.price - price) <= tol
                if na(hit)
                    hit := p
    hit

// --- PUBLIC: how many pools sit in tier `t` (active or not) -----------------
// Used by the debug table so eviction pressure is visible before it bites.
f_tierCount(int t) =>
    int n = 0
    if array.size(pools) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(pools) - 1
            if array.get(pools, i).tier == t
                n += 1
    n

// --- PUBLIC: how many pools are still active --------------------------------
activePoolCount() =>
    int n = 0
    if array.size(pools) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(pools) - 1
            if array.get(pools, i).active
                n += 1
    n

// =============================================================================
// SECTION A: SESSION ENGINE
// =============================================================================

// Resolve the London window from the preset, unless the user overrides it.
string londonPresetSess = switch londonPreset
    "Killzone 02:00-05:00" => "0200-0500"
    "Extended 02:00-06:00" => "0200-0600"
    "Legacy 03:00-07:00"   => "0300-0700"
    => "0200-0500"

string londonSession = londonUseCustom ? londonSessionCustom : londonPresetSess

// Raw membership. time() is evaluated against the bar's OPEN timestamp, which
// is fixed when the bar prints, so these flags cannot repaint intrabar.
// The RAW flags ignore the enable toggles, so range building and trading-day
// attribution stay correct even when a session is hidden.
bool inAsiaRaw   = not na(time(timeframe.period, asiaSession,    TZ))
bool inLondonRaw = not na(time(timeframe.period, londonSession,  TZ))
bool inAsiaLate  = not na(time(timeframe.period, SESS_ASIA_LATE, TZ))
bool inRthRaw    = not na(time(timeframe.period, SESS_RTH,       TZ))

// Previous-bar membership. The bar_index guard keeps bar 0 clean.
bool prevAsiaRaw   = bar_index > 0 and inAsiaRaw[1]
bool prevLondonRaw = bar_index > 0 and inLondonRaw[1]
bool prevRthRaw    = bar_index > 0 and inRthRaw[1]

// Edge transitions (raw, i.e. independent of the enable toggles).
bool asiaOpenRaw    = inAsiaRaw       and not prevAsiaRaw
bool asiaCloseRaw   = not inAsiaRaw   and prevAsiaRaw
bool londonOpenRaw  = inLondonRaw     and not prevLondonRaw
bool londonCloseRaw = not inLondonRaw and prevLondonRaw
bool rthOpenRaw     = inRthRaw        and not prevRthRaw
bool rthCloseRaw    = not inRthRaw    and prevRthRaw

// ---- PUBLIC session booleans ------------------------------------------------
bool inAsia       = asiaEnabled   and inAsiaRaw
bool inLondon     = londonEnabled and inLondonRaw
bool inAnySession = inAsia or inLondon

// Signal-eligible Asia: optionally drops the 00:00-02:00 ET tail. The RANGE is
// unaffected -- it is always built from the full asiaSession window.
bool inAsiaSignal = inAsia and not (asiaExcludeLate and inAsiaLate)

// "Just closed" fires on the FIRST CONFIRMED bar after the session ends. The
// barstate.isconfirmed gate is what stops a live bar from finalising a range.
bool asiaJustClosed   = barstate.isconfirmed and asiaCloseRaw   and asiaEnabled
bool londonJustClosed = barstate.isconfirmed and londonCloseRaw and londonEnabled

// Raw variants, so range finalisation still happens when a session is hidden.
bool asiaJustClosedRaw   = barstate.isconfirmed and asiaCloseRaw
bool londonJustClosedRaw = barstate.isconfirmed and londonCloseRaw
bool rthJustClosedRaw    = barstate.isconfirmed and rthCloseRaw

// ---- Trading-day attribution ------------------------------------------------
// Increments at the ASIA SESSION ANCHOR, never at calendar midnight. So the
// Asia session that opens Sunday 20:00 ET carries Monday's trading day.
var int tradingDay = 0
if barstate.isconfirmed and asiaOpenRaw
    tradingDay += 1

// Human-readable trading date: evening bars are labelled with the NEXT calendar
// day so the label matches the CME 18:00 ET reset.
// DST-SAFE: we do NOT add 86400000ms to the bar time. On the two US DST
// transition days the local day is 23 or 25 hours long, so a fixed 24h add
// lands on the wrong calendar date. Instead we anchor to LOCAL NOON of the
// bar's own ET date and step from there -- noon +/- 1h is still the same day,
// so the +24h step always crosses exactly one date boundary.
int etHour = hour(time, TZ)
int etNoon = timestamp(TZ, year(time, TZ), month(time, TZ), dayofmonth(time, TZ), 12, 0, 0)
int tdStamp = etHour >= TRADING_DAY_ROLL_HOUR ? etNoon + 86400000 : etNoon
string tradingDateStr = str.format_time(tdStamp, "yyyy-MM-dd", TZ)

// ---- Bars into each session --------------------------------------------------
// Reset to 1 on the session's opening bar, counted on confirmed bars only.
var int asiaBars   = 0
var int londonBars = 0
if barstate.isconfirmed
    asiaBars   := inAsiaRaw   ? (asiaOpenRaw   ? 1 : asiaBars   + 1) : 0
    londonBars := inLondonRaw ? (londonOpenRaw ? 1 : londonBars + 1) : 0

// ---- Optional background shading ---------------------------------------------
// Distinct and deliberately faint: Asia = indigo, London = amber.
bgcolor(showSessionShading and inAsia   ? color.new(color.blue,   93) : na, title = "Asia shading")
bgcolor(showSessionShading and inLondon ? color.new(color.orange, 93) : na, title = "London shading")

// =============================================================================
// SECTION B (part 2): SESSION RANGE CONTEXT
// Live range per session, completed ranges pushed into a 20-slot ring buffer,
// median read back from the buffer. Stage 5/6 use the median for exhaustion
// suppression ("this session has already travelled more than it usually does").
// =============================================================================

// Live Asia range -- ALWAYS the full asiaSession window, even when the late
// tail is muted for signals.
var float asiaCurHigh = na
var float asiaCurLow  = na
// Live London range.
var float lonCurHigh = na
var float lonCurLow  = na

if barstate.isconfirmed
    if inAsiaRaw
        asiaCurHigh := asiaOpenRaw ? high : math.max(nz(asiaCurHigh, high), high)
        asiaCurLow  := asiaOpenRaw ? low  : math.min(nz(asiaCurLow,  low),  low)
    if inLondonRaw
        lonCurHigh := londonOpenRaw ? high : math.max(nz(lonCurHigh, high), high)
        lonCurLow  := londonOpenRaw ? low  : math.min(nz(lonCurLow,  low),  low)

// Finalised Asia range, carried forward. Set when Asia closes, then held
// through London and beyond until the NEXT Asia session closes over it.
var float asiaRangeHigh = na
var float asiaRangeLow  = na

// Ring buffers of completed session ranges (max MEDIAN_LOOKBACK entries).
var array<float> asiaRangeHist   = array.new<float>()
var array<float> londonRangeHist = array.new<float>()

// Push a value, evicting the oldest once the buffer is full.
f_pushRing(array<float> a, float v) =>
    array.push(a, v)
    while array.size(a) > MEDIAN_LOOKBACK
        array.shift(a)

if asiaJustClosedRaw and not na(asiaCurHigh) and not na(asiaCurLow)
    asiaRangeHigh := asiaCurHigh
    asiaRangeLow  := asiaCurLow
    f_pushRing(asiaRangeHist, asiaCurHigh - asiaCurLow)

if londonJustClosedRaw and not na(lonCurHigh) and not na(lonCurLow)
    f_pushRing(londonRangeHist, lonCurHigh - lonCurLow)

// Medians over the last <=20 COMPLETED ranges. na until one has completed.
float asiaMedRange   = array.size(asiaRangeHist)   > 0 ? array.median(asiaRangeHist)   : na
float londonMedRange = array.size(londonRangeHist) > 0 ? array.median(londonRangeHist) : na

// Range of whichever session is live right now (na when flat).
float curSessRange = inAsiaRaw and not na(asiaCurHigh) ? asiaCurHigh - asiaCurLow :
                     inLondonRaw and not na(lonCurHigh) ? lonCurHigh - lonCurLow : na
float curSessMed = inAsiaRaw ? asiaMedRange : inLondonRaw ? londonMedRange : na

// =============================================================================
// SECTION C (part 2): HIGHER-TIMEFRAME LEVELS (PDH/PDL, PWH/PWL)
// =============================================================================

// PRIOR DAY, full session.
// WHY THE [1]: high[1]/low[1] inside the request is the daily bar that has
// ALREADY CLOSED, so the value can never change under us mid-day.
// WHY lookahead_off: without it TradingView would hand historical bars the
// completed daily value early, which is the classic backtest-flattering
// repaint. Both together are what make this safe.
[pdhFull, pdlFull] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", [high[1], low[1]],
     lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off) // [1] -> last CLOSED daily bar; lookahead_off -> no future leak

// PRIOR WEEK. Same contract: [1] = last CLOSED weekly bar, lookahead_off = no
// future leakage. Without the [1] this would return the still-forming week.
[pwhRaw, pwlRaw] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "W", [high[1], low[1]],
     lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off) // [1] -> last CLOSED weekly bar; lookahead_off -> no future leak

// PRIOR DAY, RTH only. Built natively from intraday bars -- no security call at
// all -- because a daily futures bar cannot express 09:30-16:00.
var float rthCurHigh = na
var float rthCurLow  = na
var float pdhRth     = na
var float pdlRth     = na

if barstate.isconfirmed
    if inRthRaw
        rthCurHigh := rthOpenRaw ? high : math.max(nz(rthCurHigh, high), high)
        rthCurLow  := rthOpenRaw ? low  : math.min(nz(rthCurLow,  low),  low)
    if rthJustClosedRaw and not na(rthCurHigh) and not na(rthCurLow)
        pdhRth := rthCurHigh
        pdlRth := rthCurLow

// Resolve which pair the rest of the script (and stages 2-6) treat as PDH/PDL.
float pdh = pdhlSource == "Full session" ? pdhFull : pdhRth
float pdl = pdhlSource == "Full session" ? pdlFull : pdlRth
float pwh = pwhRaw
float pwl = pwlRaw

// Period keys used to decide WHEN to restate these levels as pools.
// A value-equality test ("has the number changed?") silently fails when two
// consecutive periods share an identical high or low to the tick -- the pool
// would then never be restated for the new period. Keying off the PERIOD
// instead makes restatement unconditional and exact.
// PDH/PDL flip at the trading-day anchor (Asia open), which is precisely when
// yesterday's high stops being "today's prior day high".
int dayKey  = tradingDay
int weekKey = year(time, TZ) * 100 + weekofyear(time, TZ)

// =============================================================================
// SECTION D: SWING PIVOTS (ANTI-REPAINT)
// =============================================================================

// ta.pivothigh/low return a value only once pivotLen bars have printed to the
// RIGHT of the candidate.
// CONFIRMATION LAG IS EXACTLY pivotLen BARS: on the bar where `ph` is non-na,
// the pivot itself lives at bar_index - pivotLen. Nothing downstream is ever
// allowed to see a pivot before that bar. This lag is not a defect to be
// offset away -- it is the guarantee that the level was real.
float ph = ta.pivothigh(high, pivotLen, pivotLen)
float pl = ta.pivotlow(low,  pivotLen, pivotLen)

// Most recent CONFIRMED swings (price + TRUE bar index of the pivot).
var float lastConfirmedSwingHigh = na
var float lastConfirmedSwingLow  = na
var int   lastSwingHighBar       = na
var int   lastSwingLowBar        = na

// Short history of the last SWING_KEEP confirmed swings on each side.
var array<float> swingHighPrices = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   swingHighBars   = array.new<int>()
var array<float> swingLowPrices  = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   swingLowBars    = array.new<int>()

f_pushSwing(array<float> pxArr, array<int> ixArr, float px, int ix) =>
    array.push(pxArr, px)
    array.push(ixArr, ix)
    while array.size(pxArr) > SWING_KEEP
        array.shift(pxArr)
        array.shift(ixArr)

// =============================================================================
// SECTION C (part 3): POOL POPULATION
// Every write below sits inside the confirmed-bar gate.
// =============================================================================

// Which period each singleton level was last stated for. na = never stated.
var int pdhStatedDay  = na
var int pdlStatedDay  = na
var int pwhStatedWeek = na
var int pwlStatedWeek = na

if barstate.isconfirmed
    // ---- 1. ASIA RANGE HIGH / LOW -------------------------------------------
    // Finalised on Asia close, then carried forward through London and beyond.
    // Replaced only when the NEXT Asia session closes.
    if asiaJustClosedRaw and not na(asiaRangeHigh) and not na(asiaRangeLow)
        removePoolsByTag("Asia High")
        removePoolsByTag("Asia Low")
        f_addPool(asiaRangeHigh, "Asia High", true,  TIER_PROTECTED, showAsiaRange)
        f_addPool(asiaRangeLow,  "Asia Low",  false, TIER_PROTECTED, showAsiaRange)

    // ---- 2. PRIOR DAY HIGH / LOW --------------------------------------------
    // Restated on TRADING-DAY CHANGE, not on value change. Two consecutive days
    // can share an identical RTH high to the tick, and a value test would then
    // never restate the level.
    if not na(pdh) and (na(pdhStatedDay) or dayKey != pdhStatedDay)
        removePoolsByTag("PDH")
        f_addPool(pdh, "PDH", true, TIER_PROTECTED, showPDHL)
        pdhStatedDay := dayKey
    if not na(pdl) and (na(pdlStatedDay) or dayKey != pdlStatedDay)
        removePoolsByTag("PDL")
        f_addPool(pdl, "PDL", false, TIER_PROTECTED, showPDHL)
        pdlStatedDay := dayKey

    // ---- 3. PRIOR WEEK HIGH / LOW -------------------------------------------
    // Same defect, same fix, keyed on the calendar week instead.
    if not na(pwh) and (na(pwhStatedWeek) or weekKey != pwhStatedWeek)
        removePoolsByTag("PWH")
        f_addPool(pwh, "PWH", true, TIER_PROTECTED, showPWHL)
        pwhStatedWeek := weekKey
    if not na(pwl) and (na(pwlStatedWeek) or weekKey != pwlStatedWeek)
        removePoolsByTag("PWL")
        f_addPool(pwl, "PWL", false, TIER_PROTECTED, showPWHL)
        pwlStatedWeek := weekKey

    // ---- 4 + 5. CONFIRMED SWINGS, THEN EQUAL HIGHS / LOWS --------------------
    float tol = f_equalTol()

    if not na(ph)
        int   pbar = bar_index - pivotLen    // TRUE bar of the pivot
        float ppx  = ph

        // Cluster test runs BEFORE this pivot joins the history: how many
        // earlier confirmed swing highs sit within tolerance of it?
        int   eqCount   = 0
        float eqExtreme = ppx
        if array.size(swingHighPrices) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(swingHighPrices) - 1
                float q = array.get(swingHighPrices, i)
                if math.abs(q - ppx) <= tol
                    eqCount   += 1
                    eqExtreme := math.max(eqExtreme, q)   // extreme of the cluster

        // Register the swing itself. Stored as a pool but NOT drawn, so later
        // stages can query it without the chart turning into spaghetti.
        lastConfirmedSwingHigh := ppx
        lastSwingHighBar       := pbar
        f_pushSwing(swingHighPrices, swingHighBars, ppx, pbar)
        f_addPool(ppx, "Swing High", true, TIER_TRANSIENT, false)
        f_trimTag("Swing High", SWING_KEEP)

        // Two or more pivots inside tolerance => ONE EQH pool at the extreme.
        // If an EQH pool already covers this cluster, move it rather than add.
        Pool eqhHit = findActivePoolNear("EQH", eqExtreme, tol)
        if eqCount >= 1 and na(eqhHit)
            f_addPool(eqExtreme, "EQH", true, TIER_SIGNIFICANT, showEqualLevels)
            f_trimTag("EQH", maxEqualPools)   // per-tag cap, enforced on every add
        if eqCount >= 1 and not na(eqhHit)
            setPoolPrice(eqhHit, math.max(eqhHit.price, eqExtreme))

    if not na(pl)
        int   pbarL = bar_index - pivotLen   // TRUE bar of the pivot
        float ppxL  = pl

        int   eqCountL   = 0
        float eqExtremeL = ppxL
        if array.size(swingLowPrices) > 0
            for j = 0 to array.size(swingLowPrices) - 1
                float qL = array.get(swingLowPrices, j)
                if math.abs(qL - ppxL) <= tol
                    eqCountL   += 1
                    eqExtremeL := math.min(eqExtremeL, qL)   // extreme of the cluster

        lastConfirmedSwingLow := ppxL
        lastSwingLowBar       := pbarL
        f_pushSwing(swingLowPrices, swingLowBars, ppxL, pbarL)
        f_addPool(ppxL, "Swing Low", false, TIER_TRANSIENT, false)
        f_trimTag("Swing Low", SWING_KEEP)

        Pool eqlHit = findActivePoolNear("EQL", eqExtremeL, tol)
        if eqCountL >= 1 and na(eqlHit)
            f_addPool(eqExtremeL, "EQL", false, TIER_SIGNIFICANT, showEqualLevels)
            f_trimTag("EQL", maxEqualPools)   // per-tag cap, enforced on every add
        if eqCountL >= 1 and not na(eqlHit)
            setPoolPrice(eqlHit, math.min(eqlHit.price, eqExtremeL))

// =============================================================================
// SECTION G (STAGE 2): DISPLACEMENT
// A displacement bar is an expansion candle: unusually large range FOR ITS OWN
// RECENT CONTEXT, mostly body rather than wick, closing in the direction it
// travelled. It is the footprint of intent, and stages 3-6 use it to separate a
// real structural break from a slow drift through a level.
// =============================================================================

// Median bar range over the last dispMedianLen bars, EXCLUDING the current bar.
// The [1] is what excludes it. Without that offset a huge bar would inflate the
// very median it is being measured against and could never qualify.
float dispMedianRange = ta.median(high - low, dispMedianLen)[1]

float barRange = high - low
float barBody  = math.abs(close - open)

// The body must be a real fraction of the bar, so a huge-wick doji is rejected
// even when its total range is enormous.
bool dispBodyOk = barRange > 0 and barBody >= dispRequireBodyPct * barRange

// The two size tests, and the mode that selects between them.
bool dispAtrOk = not na(atr) and barRange >= dispAtrMult * atr
bool dispMedOk = not na(dispMedianRange) and dispMedianRange > 0 and barRange >= dispMedianMult * dispMedianRange
bool dispSizeOk = switch dispMode
    "ATR multiple"          => dispAtrOk
    "Median range multiple" => dispMedOk
    => dispAtrOk or dispMedOk

// ANTI-REPAINT: both flags are gated on barstate.isconfirmed, so a bar that
// looks like displacement mid-formation and then shrinks never announces
// itself. On the live bar both read false until the bar actually closes.
bool isDisplacementUp   = barstate.isconfirmed and dispSizeOk and dispBodyOk and close > open
bool isDisplacementDown = barstate.isconfirmed and dispSizeOk and dispBodyOk and close < open

// Most recent displacement bar in each direction. Section I uses these to test
// whether a breaking leg actually contained intent.
var int lastDispUpBar   = na
var int lastDispDownBar = na
if barstate.isconfirmed
    if isDisplacementUp
        lastDispUpBar := bar_index
    if isDisplacementDown
        lastDispDownBar := bar_index

// ---- Stage-2 label budget ---------------------------------------------------
// Every stage-2 label goes through this ring buffer, so sweep and structure
// annotations can never accumulate past MAX_S2_LABELS.
var array<label> s2Labels = array.new<label>()

f_pushS2Label(label lb) =>
    array.push(s2Labels, lb)
    while array.size(s2Labels) > MAX_S2_LABELS
        label.delete(array.shift(s2Labels))

// =============================================================================
// SECTION H (STAGE 2): LIQUIDITY SWEEP STATE MACHINE
// A sweep is not "price touched a level". It is: price cleared the level by a
// meaningful amount, then FAILED TO HOLD there. Those are two separate
// observations on two different bars, so this is modelled as an explicit state
// machine per side rather than a bundle of ad hoc flags:
//
//   (idle) --penetration--> PENETRATED --close back inside--> SWEPT
//                              |  ^
//                              |  +--UPGRADE (a more significant pool is
//                              |     penetrated while this one is pending)
//                              |
//                              +--N consecutive closes beyond--> BROKEN OUT
//                              |
//                              +--reclaim window elapsed------> EXPIRED
//
// SWEPT and BROKEN OUT both consume the pool, so one level can never produce
// two signals. EXPIRED and UPGRADE both leave the abandoned pool active.
// =============================================================================

// side          : buySide = true means BUY-side liquidity (above highs) was
//                 taken, which is a bearish/short setup. Named buySide rather
//                 than "side" to match Pool.buySide from stage 1.
// sweepExtreme  : furthest high (or low) reached while the pool was penetrated
// expiresAtBarIdx : after this bar the sweep is stale and is pruned
// mssConfirmed  : set by section I when an opposite MSS lands in time
// spent         : STAGE 6 PRIMARY DEBOUNCE. Set once this sweep has produced an
//                 entry trigger, after which it can never produce another. We
//                 debounce on the SWEEP rather than on the MSS event because a
//                 single reversal leg can legitimately fire several MSS events
//                 while structural bias lags behind it. The sweep is the setup;
//                 the MSS is only its confirmation.
type Sweep
    bool   buySide
    string poolTag
    int    poolTier
    float  poolPrice
    float  sweepExtreme
    int    confirmBarIdx
    int    expiresAtBarIdx
    bool   mssConfirmed
    bool   spent

var array<Sweep> sweeps = array.new<Sweep>()

// Resolve the significance filter to a maxTier the stage-1 pool API understands.
int sweepMaxTier = switch sweepMinTier
    "Protected only"    => TIER_PROTECTED
    "Protected + Equal" => TIER_SIGNIFICANT
    => TIER_TRANSIENT

// Penetration threshold in PRICE units, same three-mode shape as f_equalTol().
f_sweepPen() =>
    float tTicks = sweepPenTicks * syminfo.mintick
    float tAtr   = sweepPenAtrMult * nz(atr)
    float res    = switch sweepPenMode
        "Ticks" => tTicks
        "ATR"   => tAtr
        => math.max(tTicks, tAtr)
    res

// --- internal: which pool did THIS bar penetrate, above price? --------------
// CLUSTER RULE (this is the one handling rule, chosen deliberately):
// when a single bar clears several pools at once we take the MOST SIGNIFICANT
// one, i.e. the lowest tier number, breaking ties by DEEPEST penetration.
// WHY: equal highs habitually form a few points under a session high, so a
// "nearest one wins" rule would hand the sweep to the EQH and stage 5 would
// score it with poolWeight(1) = 0.6 instead of poolWeight(0) = 1.0. Taking the
// most significant level keeps the score honest. Pools that were penetrated but
// not selected stay ACTIVE and remain valid targets on a later bar.
// `refPx` is the previous confirmed close: the pool must have been ABOVE us
// before this bar, otherwise clearing its price is not taking resting
// liquidity, it is just continuing a move we were already inside.
f_sweepTargetAbove(float barHigh, float refPx, float pen, int maxTier) =>
    Pool best = na
    if array.size(pools) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(pools) - 1
            Pool p = array.get(pools, i)
            if p.active and p.buySide and p.tier <= maxTier and p.price > refPx and barHigh >= p.price + pen
                if na(best)
                    best := p
                else if p.tier < best.tier
                    best := p
                else if p.tier == best.tier and p.price < best.price
                    best := p                       // lower price = deeper penetration
    best

// --- internal: mirror of the above, below price -----------------------------
f_sweepTargetBelow(float barLow, float refPx, float pen, int maxTier) =>
    Pool best = na
    if array.size(pools) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(pools) - 1
            Pool p = array.get(pools, i)
            if p.active and not p.buySide and p.tier <= maxTier and p.price < refPx and barLow <= p.price - pen
                if na(best)
                    best := p
                else if p.tier < best.tier
                    best := p
                else if p.tier == best.tier and p.price > best.price
                    best := p                       // higher price = deeper penetration
    best

// --- internal: retire a pool and show that it is retired --------------------
// The line stays on the chart but goes dashed and grey, and the label gains an
// "x", so a consumed level is visually distinct from a live one.
f_markPoolConsumed(Pool p) =>
    p.active := false
    if not na(p.ln)
        line.set_style(p.ln, line.style_dashed)
        line.set_color(p.ln, color.new(color.gray, 70))
    if not na(p.lb)
        label.set_text(p.lb, "x " + p.tag)
        label.set_textcolor(p.lb, color.new(color.gray, 40))

// --- internal: drop stale sweeps, then cap the book -------------------------
f_pruneSweeps() =>
    if array.size(sweeps) > 0
        for i = array.size(sweeps) - 1 to 0
            if bar_index > array.get(sweeps, i).expiresAtBarIdx
                array.remove(sweeps, i)
    while array.size(sweeps) > MAX_SWEEPS
        array.shift(sweeps)

// --- PUBLIC: most recent unexpired sweep on `buySide`, or na ----------------
// Iterating backwards means the first match found is the newest.
getLiveSweep(bool buySide) =>
    Sweep best = na
    if array.size(sweeps) > 0
        for i = array.size(sweeps) - 1 to 0
            Sweep sw = array.get(sweeps, i)
            if na(best) and sw.buySide == buySide and bar_index <= sw.expiresAtBarIdx
                best := sw
    best

// --- PUBLIC: is there a live sweep on this side that an MSS has confirmed? --
// isSweepMssPair(false) = LONG setup  (sell-side liquidity taken, then bullish MSS)
// isSweepMssPair(true)  = SHORT setup (buy-side liquidity taken, then bearish MSS)
isSweepMssPair(bool buySide) =>
    Sweep sw = getLiveSweep(buySide)
    bool ok = false
    if not na(sw)
        ok := sw.mssConfirmed
    ok

// ---- Pending penetration state, one per side --------------------------------
// We store the Pool OBJECT, not its array index. The book is mutated between
// bars (eviction, re-statement), so an index would go stale; a Pine object
// reference stays valid even after the pool leaves the array.
var Pool  pendUpPool    = na
var int   pendUpBar     = na
var float pendUpExtreme = na
var int   pendUpCloses  = 0

var Pool  pendDnPool    = na
var int   pendDnBar     = na
var float pendDnExtreme = na
var int   pendDnCloses  = 0

// Cumulative calibration counters for the debug table.
var int sweepConfirmedCount   = 0
var int breakoutRejectedCount = 0
var int sweepUpgradeCount     = 0      // how often a pending record was upgraded
var int lastBreakoutDir       = 0      // +1 up, -1 down. For later stages.

// Per-bar marker prices. Not `var`, so they reset to na every bar.
float sweepUpMarkPx = na
float sweepDnMarkPx = na

if barstate.isconfirmed
    // ---- 0a. Carry the previous Asia range into the live Asia session -------
    // We REPLACE the old "Asia High"/"Asia Low" pools rather than adding
    // alongside them: they sit at exactly the same prices, so adding would
    // draw two lines on top of each other. Re-stating also resets `active`,
    // so a level consumed during London or RTH is a valid target again for
    // the new Asia session.
    if carryPriorAsiaRange and asiaOpenRaw and not na(asiaRangeHigh) and not na(asiaRangeLow)
        removePoolsByTag("Asia High")
        removePoolsByTag("Asia Low")
        removePoolsByTag("Prior Asia High")
        removePoolsByTag("Prior Asia Low")
        f_addPool(asiaRangeHigh, "Prior Asia High", true,  TIER_PROTECTED, showAsiaRange)
        f_addPool(asiaRangeLow,  "Prior Asia Low",  false, TIER_PROTECTED, showAsiaRange)

    // ---- 0b. Asia closed: stage 1 has already stated the NEW Asia range
    //          earlier on this same bar, so the carried pools are superseded.
    if asiaJustClosedRaw
        removePoolsByTag("Prior Asia High")
        removePoolsByTag("Prior Asia Low")

    f_pruneSweeps()
    float pen = f_sweepPen()

    // =========================== BUY-SIDE (highs) ===========================
    // 1. PENETRATE or UPGRADE.
    //    f_sweepTargetAbove is evaluated on EVERY confirmed bar, not only when
    //    the side is idle. That second case matters: on a fast push price can
    //    clear a minor EQH on one bar and the Asia High a bar or two later, and
    //    by then the Asia High sits BELOW close[1] so the `p.price > refPx`
    //    guard would make it unreachable forever. The pending record would be
    //    stuck on the minor level -- exactly the setup we most want to catch,
    //    shadowed by the least significant pool involved.
    if not na(close[1])
        Pool tgtUp = f_sweepTargetAbove(high, close[1], pen, sweepMaxTier)

        // 1a. Fresh penetration: nothing was pending on this side.
        if not na(tgtUp) and na(pendUpPool)
            pendUpPool    := tgtUp
            pendUpBar     := bar_index
            pendUpExtreme := high
            pendUpCloses  := 0

        // 1b. UPGRADE: a STRICTLY more significant pool was penetrated while a
        //     record was already pending. Equal tier does not upgrade -- only a
        //     lower tier number, so this can fire at most twice per pending
        //     record (T2 -> T1 -> T0) and cannot oscillate.
        //     WHY THE CLOCKS RESTART: the more significant level was penetrated
        //     on THIS bar, so its reclaim window has to be measured from here,
        //     not inherited from when the minor level was poked. Same for the
        //     breakout count -- closes beyond the EQH say nothing about whether
        //     the Asia High is holding. The extreme is the one thing carried
        //     forward, because the furthest price reached is a property of the
        //     whole excursion, not of which level we happen to be tracking.
        //     The abandoned pool is NOT consumed: it stays active and can be
        //     penetrated again on a later approach.
        if not na(tgtUp) and not na(pendUpPool) and tgtUp.tier < pendUpPool.tier
            pendUpExtreme := math.max(nz(pendUpExtreme, high), high)
            pendUpPool    := tgtUp
            pendUpBar     := bar_index
            pendUpCloses  := 0
            sweepUpgradeCount += 1

    // 2. Evaluate the pending record. This deliberately runs on the penetration
    //    bar as well, so a single bar that pokes above and closes back below --
    //    the canonical rejection wick -- confirms immediately instead of
    //    waiting a bar it does not need.
    if not na(pendUpPool)
        pendUpExtreme := math.max(pendUpExtreme, high)
        pendUpCloses  := close > pendUpPool.price ? pendUpCloses + 1 : 0
        int   ageUp     = bar_index - pendUpBar
        // The reclaim window and the breakout window are DECOUPLED on purpose.
        // A reclaim only counts inside sweepReclaimBars, but the record has to
        // stay alive long enough for breakoutClosesToInvalidate consecutive
        // closes to accumulate -- otherwise setting, say, reclaim = 1 and
        // breakout = 4 would make a breakout literally unreachable and the
        // sweep:breakout ratio in the debug table would be meaningless.
        int   holdUp    = math.max(sweepReclaimBars, breakoutClosesToInvalidate - 1)
        bool  brokeUp   = pendUpCloses >= breakoutClosesToInvalidate
        bool  reclaimUp = close < pendUpPool.price and ageUp <= sweepReclaimBars
        bool  expireUp  = ageUp > holdUp

        // BREAKOUT: the level did not hold. Consume it so it cannot later also
        // register as a sweep, and remember the direction for later stages.
        if brokeUp
            f_markPoolConsumed(pendUpPool)
            breakoutRejectedCount += 1
            lastBreakoutDir := 1
            pendUpPool := na

        // SWEEP CONFIRMED.
        if not brokeUp and reclaimUp
            f_markPoolConsumed(pendUpPool)
            sweepConfirmedCount += 1
            array.push(sweeps, Sweep.new(buySide = true, poolTag = pendUpPool.tag,
                     poolTier = pendUpPool.tier, poolPrice = pendUpPool.price,
                     sweepExtreme = pendUpExtreme, confirmBarIdx = bar_index,
                     expiresAtBarIdx = bar_index + sweepValidBars, mssConfirmed = false,
                     spent = false))
            sweepUpMarkPx := pendUpExtreme
            if showSweepMarkers
                f_pushS2Label(label.new(bar_index, pendUpExtreme, "swept: " + pendUpPool.tag,
                         xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_down,
                         color = color.new(colBuySide, 82), textcolor = color.new(colBuySide, 0),
                         size = size.tiny))
            pendUpPool := na

        // EXPIRED: neither reclaimed in time nor decisively broken. Leave the
        // pool ACTIVE. If price is still above it, the `p.price > refPx` guard
        // in f_sweepTargetAbove stops it re-triggering until price comes back
        // below and pokes through again.
        if not brokeUp and not reclaimUp and expireUp
            pendUpPool := na

    // =========================== SELL-SIDE (lows) ===========================
    // Exact mirror of the buy-side penetrate/upgrade logic above; see there for
    // why the age clock and breakout count restart on an upgrade.
    if not na(close[1])
        Pool tgtDn = f_sweepTargetBelow(low, close[1], pen, sweepMaxTier)

        // 1a. Fresh penetration.
        if not na(tgtDn) and na(pendDnPool)
            pendDnPool    := tgtDn
            pendDnBar     := bar_index
            pendDnExtreme := low
            pendDnCloses  := 0

        // 1b. UPGRADE to a strictly more significant pool.
        if not na(tgtDn) and not na(pendDnPool) and tgtDn.tier < pendDnPool.tier
            pendDnExtreme := math.min(nz(pendDnExtreme, low), low)
            pendDnPool    := tgtDn
            pendDnBar     := bar_index
            pendDnCloses  := 0
            sweepUpgradeCount += 1

    if not na(pendDnPool)
        pendDnExtreme := math.min(pendDnExtreme, low)
        pendDnCloses  := close < pendDnPool.price ? pendDnCloses + 1 : 0
        int   ageDn     = bar_index - pendDnBar
        int   holdDn    = math.max(sweepReclaimBars, breakoutClosesToInvalidate - 1)
        bool  brokeDn   = pendDnCloses >= breakoutClosesToInvalidate
        bool  reclaimDn = close > pendDnPool.price and ageDn <= sweepReclaimBars
        bool  expireDn  = ageDn > holdDn

        if brokeDn
            f_markPoolConsumed(pendDnPool)
            breakoutRejectedCount += 1
            lastBreakoutDir := -1
            pendDnPool := na

        if not brokeDn and reclaimDn
            f_markPoolConsumed(pendDnPool)
            sweepConfirmedCount += 1
            array.push(sweeps, Sweep.new(buySide = false, poolTag = pendDnPool.tag,
                     poolTier = pendDnPool.tier, poolPrice = pendDnPool.price,
                     sweepExtreme = pendDnExtreme, confirmBarIdx = bar_index,
                     expiresAtBarIdx = bar_index + sweepValidBars, mssConfirmed = false,
                     spent = false))
            sweepDnMarkPx := pendDnExtreme
            if showSweepMarkers
                f_pushS2Label(label.new(bar_index, pendDnExtreme, "swept: " + pendDnPool.tag,
                         xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_up,
                         color = color.new(colSellSide, 82), textcolor = color.new(colSellSide, 0),
                         size = size.tiny))
            pendDnPool := na

        if not brokeDn and not reclaimDn and expireDn
            pendDnPool := na

// =============================================================================
// SECTION I (STAGE 2): BOS / CHoCH / MSS
//
// ANTI-REPAINT PROOF -- why a break can never be registered against a swing
// that was not yet confirmed when the break happened:
//   lastConfirmedSwingHigh / lastConfirmedSwingLow are written by stage 1 ONLY
//   inside `if barstate.isconfirmed` and ONLY on a bar where ta.pivothigh /
//   ta.pivotlow returned non-na. That bar is, by construction, pivotLen bars
//   AFTER the pivot bar itself. So at any bar B those variables can only hold a
//   pivot whose confirmation bar is <= B, i.e. whose pivot bar is <= B-pivotLen.
//   This section reads nothing else -- no ta.pivot* call of its own, no history
//   offset into the future, no `[-n]` -- so the value it compares close against
//   was already public knowledge at bar B's close.
//   The degenerate case is also safe: a pivot high confirmed ON bar B cannot be
//   broken by bar B, because ta.pivothigh only returns it if the following
//   pivotLen highs (bar B's included) are all below it, hence close < pivot.
// =============================================================================

// Swing sequence state. +1 = higher than the previous swing on that side,
// -1 = lower, 0 = not yet known.
var int   highSeq         = 0
var int   lowSeq          = 0
var float prevSwingHighPx = na
var float prevSwingLowPx  = na

// Structural bias: +1 bull, -1 bear, 0 neutral. Derived ONLY from the HH/HL vs
// LH/LL sequence, never from the break events themselves.
var int structBias = 0

// Last structure event, for the debug table and later stages.
var string lastStructType = ""     // "BOS" / "CHoCH" / "MSS"
var int    lastStructDir  = 0      // +1 break up, -1 break down
var int    lastStructBar  = na

// Which swing has already been broken, keyed by its TRUE pivot bar index. This
// is what makes CHoCH the FIRST close beyond a swing rather than every close.
var int brokenSwingHighBar = na
var int brokenSwingLowBar  = na

f_structColor(string kind) =>
    color c = switch kind
        "BOS"   => colBOS
        "CHoCH" => colCHoCH
        => colMSS
    c

if barstate.isconfirmed
    // ---- 1. Swing sequence -> structural bias -------------------------------
    if not na(ph)
        if not na(prevSwingHighPx)
            highSeq := ph > prevSwingHighPx ? 1 : ph < prevSwingHighPx ? -1 : highSeq
        prevSwingHighPx := ph
    if not na(pl)
        if not na(prevSwingLowPx)
            lowSeq := pl > prevSwingLowPx ? 1 : pl < prevSwingLowPx ? -1 : lowSeq
        prevSwingLowPx := pl
    structBias := highSeq > 0 and lowSeq > 0 ? 1 : highSeq < 0 and lowSeq < 0 ? -1 : 0

    // ---- 2. Break detection --------------------------------------------------
    // The na() guards on the "already broken" trackers matter: in Pine an
    // int != na comparison yields na, not true, which would suppress the very
    // first break of the chart.
    bool brokeHigh = not na(lastConfirmedSwingHigh) and close > lastConfirmedSwingHigh and (na(brokenSwingHighBar) or lastSwingHighBar != brokenSwingHighBar)
    bool brokeLow  = not na(lastConfirmedSwingLow)  and close < lastConfirmedSwingLow  and (na(brokenSwingLowBar)  or lastSwingLowBar  != brokenSwingLowBar)

    // ---- 3. Classify an UP break --------------------------------------------
    if brokeHigh
        brokenSwingHighBar := lastSwingHighBar
        // Continuation only when bias is ALREADY bullish. Neutral bias counts
        // as a change of character: with no established trend, the first close
        // beyond a confirmed swing IS the structural statement.
        bool contUp = structBias > 0
        // Breaking leg = from the broken swing's own bar to this bar. A
        // displacement up anywhere inside that window means the break carried
        // intent rather than drifting through.
        bool legDispUp = not na(lastDispUpBar) and lastDispUpBar >= lastSwingHighBar
        string kindUp = contUp ? "BOS" : (requireDisplacementForMSS ? (legDispUp ? "MSS" : "CHoCH") : "MSS")
        lastStructType := kindUp
        lastStructDir  := 1
        lastStructBar  := bar_index
        // A bullish MSS pairs with a SELL-side sweep: lows taken, then up.
        if kindUp == "MSS"
            Sweep swUp = getLiveSweep(false)
            if not na(swUp) and bar_index - swUp.confirmBarIdx <= mssMaxBarsAfterSweep
                swUp.mssConfirmed := true
        if showStructureLabels
            f_pushS2Label(label.new(bar_index, high, kindUp,
                     xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_down,
                     color = color.new(f_structColor(kindUp), 82),
                     textcolor = f_structColor(kindUp), size = size.tiny))

    // ---- 4. Classify a DOWN break -------------------------------------------
    if brokeLow
        brokenSwingLowBar := lastSwingLowBar
        bool contDn = structBias < 0
        bool legDispDn = not na(lastDispDownBar) and lastDispDownBar >= lastSwingLowBar
        string kindDn = contDn ? "BOS" : (requireDisplacementForMSS ? (legDispDn ? "MSS" : "CHoCH") : "MSS")
        lastStructType := kindDn
        lastStructDir  := -1
        lastStructBar  := bar_index
        // A bearish MSS pairs with a BUY-side sweep: highs taken, then down.
        if kindDn == "MSS"
            Sweep swDn = getLiveSweep(true)
            if not na(swDn) and bar_index - swDn.confirmBarIdx <= mssMaxBarsAfterSweep
                swDn.mssConfirmed := true
        if showStructureLabels
            f_pushS2Label(label.new(bar_index, low, kindDn,
                     xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_up,
                     color = color.new(f_structColor(kindDn), 82),
                     textcolor = f_structColor(kindDn), size = size.tiny))

// ---- Keep pool labels pinned near the right edge ----------------------------
// Only on the last bar, so historical bars do no drawing work at all.
if barstate.islast and array.size(pools) > 0
    for i = 0 to array.size(pools) - 1
        Pool p = array.get(pools, i)
        if p.active and not na(p.lb)
            label.set_x(p.lb, bar_index + 3)

// ---- Confirmed swing markers -------------------------------------------------
// Drawn back at the TRUE pivot bar via offset, but they only APPEAR pivotLen
// bars later. That visible delay is the anti-repaint behaviour, on purpose.
plotshape(showSwingMarkers and not na(ph), title = "Confirmed swing high",
     style = shape.triangledown, location = location.abovebar, offset = -pivotLen,
     color = color.new(colBuySide, 20), size = size.tiny)
plotshape(showSwingMarkers and not na(pl), title = "Confirmed swing low",
     style = shape.triangleup, location = location.belowbar, offset = -pivotLen,
     color = color.new(colSellSide, 20), size = size.tiny)

// =============================================================================
// SECTION J (STAGE 2): VISUALS
// Sweep crosses are PLOTS, not drawing objects, so they cost nothing against
// the 500-object ceiling. The text labels beside them, and the structure
// labels, go through the s2Labels ring buffer instead.
// =============================================================================

// Displacement bar highlight. Because isDisplacement* are confirmed-bar gated,
// the live bar stays its normal colour until it closes -- if it recolours on
// close, that is the anti-repaint gate doing its job, not a glitch.
barcolor(showDisplacement and isDisplacementUp   ? colDispUp :
         showDisplacement and isDisplacementDown ? colDispDown : na,
     title = "Displacement bar")

// The "x" sits at the sweep extreme -- the furthest price reached while the
// pool was penetrated -- drawn on the bar the sweep was CONFIRMED.
plotshape(showSweepMarkers ? sweepUpMarkPx : na, title = "Buy-side sweep",
     style = shape.xcross, location = location.absolute,
     color = color.new(colBuySide, 0), size = size.tiny)
plotshape(showSweepMarkers ? sweepDnMarkPx : na, title = "Sell-side sweep",
     style = shape.xcross, location = location.absolute,
     color = color.new(colSellSide, 0), size = size.tiny)

// =============================================================================
// SECTION K (STAGE 3): ZONE TYPES AND SHARED HELPERS
// =============================================================================

// --- FAIR VALUE GAP ----------------------------------------------------------
// ce       : midpoint. The level stage 5 keys on.
// inverted : this gap has already spawned an inverse FVG. Latch so one gap can
//            never produce two of them.
// bx/ceLn  : its drawing objects, carried on the record as stage 1 does.
type FVG
    float top
    float bottom
    float ce
    bool  bullish
    int   createdBar
    int   expiresBar
    int   state
    bool  inverted
    box   bx   = na
    line  ceLn = na

// --- INVERSE FVG -------------------------------------------------------------
// DESIGN DECISION: a SEPARATE TYPE, not a flag on FVG.
// A flag would leave one object simultaneously INVALIDATED as an FVG and FRESH
// as an IFVG, holding two polarities and two expiry clocks at once -- a state
// machine with two heads, where every consumer has to remember to apply the
// polarity flip or read the right clock. Splitting them keeps each record's
// invariants true of itself: the dead FVG stays an honest record of what
// failed, and the IFVG starts a clean life with its own age limit.
type IFVG
    float top
    float bottom
    float ce
    bool  bullish        // ALREADY FLIPPED relative to the parent gap
    int   createdBar
    int   expiresBar
    int   state
    box   bx = na

// --- ORDER BLOCK -------------------------------------------------------------
// mitigated : price returned into the zone AND closed back on the correct side,
//             i.e. it was defended at least once.
// fromMss   : created by an MSS rather than a plain BOS. Recorded at creation
//             because provenance cannot be recovered later.
type OB
    float top
    float bottom
    bool  bullish
    int   anchorBar
    int   createdBar
    int   expiresBar
    int   state
    bool  mitigated
    bool  fromMss
    box   bx = na

// --- UNIFIED POINT OF INTEREST -----------------------------------------------
// The ONE thing stage 5 queries. kind is diagnostic only: an FVG and an order
// block left by the same displacement leg are the same observation seen twice,
// and scoring both would pay the model twice for one piece of evidence.
// inOte / fromMssLeg are surfaced because bestPOI ranks on them and stage 5
// may want to explain its own score.
type POI
    float  top
    float  bottom
    float  ce
    bool   bullish
    string kind          // "FVG" / "IFVG" / "OB" / "BREAKER"
    float  quality       // 0-1, see f_poiQuality
    int    sourceBar
    bool   inOte
    bool   fromMssLeg

var array<FVG>  fvgs    = array.new<FVG>()
var array<IFVG> ifvgs   = array.new<IFVG>()
var array<OB>   obs     = array.new<OB>()
var array<POI>  poiBook = array.new<POI>()

// How often a newly created zone landed on top of an existing zone of the other
// kind. Surfaced in the debug table -- see the notes on collinearity above.
var int fvgObCoincidenceCount = 0

// CUMULATIVE creation counters. The table shows these beside the ACTIVE counts,
// because "0 active FVGs" is ambiguous on its own: it could mean a quiet moment
// or it could mean FVGs essentially never form. Only the pair distinguishes
// those two, and they demand completely different responses.
var int cumFvgBull  = 0
var int cumFvgBear  = 0
var int cumIfvg     = 0
var int cumOb       = 0
var int cumBreaker  = 0

// --- shared: retire a zone's drawings ---------------------------------------
// Fade rather than delete, for the same reason retired liquidity pools stay on
// the chart: where a zone failed is information.
f_retireBox(box bx) =>
    if not na(bx) and fadeInvalidated
        box.set_extend(bx, extend.none)
        box.set_right(bx, bar_index)
        box.set_bgcolor(bx, color.new(colDead, 90))
        box.set_border_color(bx, color.new(colDead, 55))
    if not na(bx) and not fadeInvalidated
        box.delete(bx)

f_retireLine(line ln) =>
    if not na(ln) and fadeInvalidated
        line.set_extend(ln, extend.none)
        line.set_x2(ln, bar_index)
        line.set_color(ln, color.new(colDead, 70))
    if not na(ln) and not fadeInvalidated
        line.delete(ln)

// --- shared: caps, oldest first ----------------------------------------------
f_capFvgs() =>
    while array.size(fvgs) > MAX_FVGS
        FVG g = array.shift(fvgs)
        if not na(g.bx)
            box.delete(g.bx)
        if not na(g.ceLn)
            line.delete(g.ceLn)

f_capIfvgs() =>
    while array.size(ifvgs) > MAX_IFVGS
        IFVG g = array.shift(ifvgs)
        if not na(g.bx)
            box.delete(g.bx)

f_capObs() =>
    while array.size(obs) > MAX_OBS
        OB o = array.shift(obs)
        if not na(o.bx)
            box.delete(o.bx)

// --- shared: interval intersection with a tolerance --------------------------
f_poiTol() =>
    float t = poiOverlapTolTicks * syminfo.mintick
    t

f_zonesOverlap(float t1, float b1, float t2, float b2, float tol) =>
    bool r = (b1 - tol) <= t2 and (t1 + tol) >= b2
    r

// --- shared: does this zone sit on top of a live zone of the other kind? -----
f_fvgCoincidesWithOb(float top, float bottom, bool bullish) =>
    bool r = false
    float tol = f_poiTol()
    if array.size(obs) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(obs) - 1
            OB o = array.get(obs, i)
            if not r and o.state <= ST_CE_TAGGED and o.bullish == bullish and f_zonesOverlap(top, bottom, o.top, o.bottom, tol)
                r := true
    r

f_obCoincidesWithFvg(float top, float bottom, bool bullish) =>
    bool r = false
    float tol = f_poiTol()
    if array.size(fvgs) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(fvgs) - 1
            FVG g = array.get(fvgs, i)
            if not r and g.state <= ST_CE_TAGGED and g.bullish == bullish and f_zonesOverlap(top, bottom, g.top, g.bottom, tol)
                r := true
    r

// =============================================================================
// SECTION L (STAGE 3): FAIR VALUE GAPS + INVERSE FVGs
// A three-candle imbalance: the wick of candle 1 and the wick of candle 3 never
// met, so a band of price was skipped. On its own that is just a printing
// artefact, which is why the middle candle is required to be displacement --
// then the gap is the signature of someone lifting through the book.
// =============================================================================

f_fvgMinSize() =>
    float tTicks = fvgMinTicks * syminfo.mintick
    float tAtr   = fvgMinAtrMult * nz(atr)
    float res    = switch fvgMinMode
        "Ticks" => tTicks
        "ATR"   => tAtr
        => math.max(tTicks, tAtr)
    res

if barstate.isconfirmed
    // ---- 1. STATE MACHINE for existing gaps ---------------------------------
    // Runs before creation, so a gap can never be created and transitioned on
    // the same bar off its own third candle.
    if array.size(fvgs) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(fvgs) - 1
            FVG g = array.get(fvgs, i)

            // Expiry applies to any gap that has not already aged out, including
            // INVALIDATED ones -- otherwise a dead gap would linger forever as
            // an inverse-FVG candidate.
            if g.state != ST_EXPIRED and bar_index > g.expiresBar
                if g.state <= ST_CE_TAGGED
                    f_retireBox(g.bx)
                    f_retireLine(g.ceLn)
                g.state := ST_EXPIRED

            // Live transitions. Invalidation is tested first: once the gap has
            // failed, a touch or CE tag on the same bar is meaningless.
            if g.state <= ST_CE_TAGGED
                bool inval = false
                if g.bullish
                    inval := fvgInvalidateOn == "Full fill" ? low <= g.bottom :
                             fvgInvalidateOn == "CE breach" ? low <= g.ce : close < g.bottom
                if not g.bullish
                    inval := fvgInvalidateOn == "Full fill" ? high >= g.top :
                             fvgInvalidateOn == "CE breach" ? high >= g.ce : close > g.top

                if inval
                    g.state := ST_INVALIDATED
                    f_retireBox(g.bx)
                    f_retireLine(g.ceLn)

                // Touch / CE tag, most advanced first so one bar can jump two
                // states. State only ever moves forward.
                if not inval and g.bullish and low <= g.ce and g.state < ST_CE_TAGGED
                    g.state := ST_CE_TAGGED
                if not inval and g.bullish and low <= g.top and g.state < ST_TOUCHED
                    g.state := ST_TOUCHED
                if not inval and not g.bullish and high >= g.ce and g.state < ST_CE_TAGGED
                    g.state := ST_CE_TAGGED
                if not inval and not g.bullish and high >= g.bottom and g.state < ST_TOUCHED
                    g.state := ST_TOUCHED

            // ---- 2. INVERSE FVG conversion -----------------------------------
            // Deliberately evaluated even when the gap is ALREADY invalidated:
            // under "Full fill" a wick can kill the gap on one bar while the
            // decisive body close arrives a bar or two later, and that close is
            // the event that flips polarity. The `inverted` latch keeps it to
            // one conversion per gap.
            if not g.inverted and g.state != ST_EXPIRED
                bool through = false
                if g.bullish
                    through := ifvgRequireCloseThrough ? close < g.bottom : low < g.bottom
                if not g.bullish
                    through := ifvgRequireCloseThrough ? close > g.top : high > g.top
                if through
                    g.inverted := true
                    if g.state <= ST_CE_TAGGED
                        g.state := ST_INVALIDATED
                        f_retireBox(g.bx)
                        f_retireLine(g.ceLn)
                    // Same coordinates, OPPOSITE polarity: a failed bearish gap
                    // is now support, a failed bullish gap is now resistance.
                    bool ivBull = not g.bullish
                    IFVG iv = IFVG.new(top = g.top, bottom = g.bottom, ce = g.ce,
                             bullish = ivBull, createdBar = bar_index,
                             expiresBar = bar_index + ifvgMaxAgeBars, state = ST_FRESH)
                    if showIFVG
                        color ic = ivBull ? colIfvgBull : colIfvgBear
                        iv.bx := box.new(bar_index, g.top, bar_index + 1, g.bottom,
                                 xloc = xloc.bar_index, extend = extend.right,
                                 bgcolor = color.new(ic, 88),
                                 border_color = color.new(ic, 40),
                                 border_width = 1, border_style = line.style_solid)
                    array.push(ifvgs, iv)
                    cumIfvg += 1
                    f_capIfvgs()

    // ---- 3. CREATION --------------------------------------------------------
    // Three-candle definition, read off CONFIRMED bars only. bar_index >= 2
    // guards the history access.
    if bar_index >= 2
        float minSz = f_fvgMinSize()

        // Bullish: candle 1's high never met candle 3's low.
        bool bullGap = high[2] < low
        if bullGap
            float gTop = low
            float gBot = high[2]
            bool szOk   = (gTop - gBot) >= minSz
            bool dispOk = not fvgRequireDisplacement or isDisplacementUp[1]
            if szOk and dispOk
                float gCe = (gTop + gBot) / 2
                bool coi = f_fvgCoincidesWithOb(gTop, gBot, true)
                cumFvgBull += 1
                if coi
                    fvgObCoincidenceCount += 1
                FVG g = FVG.new(top = gTop, bottom = gBot, ce = gCe, bullish = true,
                         createdBar = bar_index, expiresBar = bar_index + fvgMaxAgeBars,
                         state = ST_FRESH, inverted = false)
                if showFVG
                    g.bx := box.new(bar_index - 2, gTop, bar_index + 1, gBot,
                             xloc = xloc.bar_index, extend = extend.right,
                             bgcolor = color.new(colFvgBull, 90),
                             border_color = color.new(colFvgBull, 55),
                             border_width = 1, border_style = line.style_dotted)
                    g.ceLn := line.new(bar_index - 2, gCe, bar_index + 1, gCe,
                             xloc = xloc.bar_index, extend = extend.right,
                             color = color.new(colFvgBull, 35),
                             style = line.style_dashed, width = 1)
                array.push(fvgs, g)
                f_capFvgs()

        // Bearish: candle 1's low never met candle 3's high.
        bool bearGap = low[2] > high
        if bearGap
            float gTopB = low[2]
            float gBotB = high
            bool szOkB   = (gTopB - gBotB) >= minSz
            bool dispOkB = not fvgRequireDisplacement or isDisplacementDown[1]
            if szOkB and dispOkB
                float gCeB = (gTopB + gBotB) / 2
                bool coiB = f_fvgCoincidesWithOb(gTopB, gBotB, false)
                cumFvgBear += 1
                if coiB
                    fvgObCoincidenceCount += 1
                FVG gb = FVG.new(top = gTopB, bottom = gBotB, ce = gCeB, bullish = false,
                         createdBar = bar_index, expiresBar = bar_index + fvgMaxAgeBars,
                         state = ST_FRESH, inverted = false)
                if showFVG
                    gb.bx := box.new(bar_index - 2, gTopB, bar_index + 1, gBotB,
                             xloc = xloc.bar_index, extend = extend.right,
                             bgcolor = color.new(colFvgBear, 90),
                             border_color = color.new(colFvgBear, 55),
                             border_width = 1, border_style = line.style_dotted)
                    gb.ceLn := line.new(bar_index - 2, gCeB, bar_index + 1, gCeB,
                             xloc = xloc.bar_index, extend = extend.right,
                             color = color.new(colFvgBear, 35),
                             style = line.style_dashed, width = 1)
                array.push(fvgs, gb)
                f_capFvgs()

    // ---- 4. INVERSE FVG state machine ---------------------------------------
    // Simpler than the gap it came from: an IFVG is a level that already proved
    // it flips, so it only tracks touch, CE tag, close-through death and age.
    if array.size(ifvgs) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(ifvgs) - 1
            IFVG iv = array.get(ifvgs, i)
            if iv.state != ST_EXPIRED and bar_index > iv.expiresBar
                if iv.state <= ST_CE_TAGGED
                    f_retireBox(iv.bx)
                iv.state := ST_EXPIRED
            if iv.state <= ST_CE_TAGGED
                bool ivDead = iv.bullish ? close < iv.bottom : close > iv.top
                if ivDead
                    iv.state := ST_INVALIDATED
                    f_retireBox(iv.bx)
                if not ivDead and iv.bullish and low <= iv.ce and iv.state < ST_CE_TAGGED
                    iv.state := ST_CE_TAGGED
                if not ivDead and iv.bullish and low <= iv.top and iv.state < ST_TOUCHED
                    iv.state := ST_TOUCHED
                if not ivDead and not iv.bullish and high >= iv.ce and iv.state < ST_CE_TAGGED
                    iv.state := ST_CE_TAGGED
                if not ivDead and not iv.bullish and high >= iv.bottom and iv.state < ST_TOUCHED
                    iv.state := ST_TOUCHED

// =============================================================================
// SECTION M (STAGE 3): ORDER BLOCKS / BREAKERS
// DISPLACEMENT-ANCHORED definition. Not "the last down candle before an up
// move", which fires on every second bar and means nothing. A block only
// exists if the leg that left it BROKE STRUCTURE.
//
// ANTI-REPAINT, INHERITED: creation is triggered by stage 2's BOS/MSS events.
// Those fire only inside `if barstate.isconfirmed`, and only against
// lastConfirmedSwingHigh / lastConfirmedSwingLow, which stage 1 writes only on
// a pivot CONFIRMATION bar -- pivotLen bars after the pivot itself. So an order
// block can never be anchored to a leg whose break was not already public
// knowledge at the close of the bar that created it. The backward hunt for the
// anchor candle reads close[k]/open[k], which are settled history.
// =============================================================================

if barstate.isconfirmed
    // ---- 1. STATE MACHINE ---------------------------------------------------
    if array.size(obs) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(obs) - 1
            OB o = array.get(obs, i)

            if o.state != ST_EXPIRED and bar_index > o.expiresBar
                if o.state <= ST_CE_TAGGED or o.state == ST_BREAKER
                    f_retireBox(o.bx)
                o.state := ST_EXPIRED

            if o.state <= ST_CE_TAGGED
                // A body close beyond the far edge does not merely kill the
                // block, it INVERTS it: the orders that were supposed to defend
                // this level are now trapped on the wrong side.
                bool through = o.bullish ? close < o.bottom : close > o.top
                bool flips   = obInvalidateOnCloseThrough and through
                if flips
                    o.state := ST_BREAKER
                    cumBreaker += 1
                    if not na(o.bx)
                        box.set_bgcolor(o.bx, color.new(colBreaker, 88))
                        box.set_border_color(o.bx, color.new(colBreaker, 35))
                        box.set_border_style(o.bx, line.style_dashed)

                // Mitigation: price came back INTO the zone and still closed on
                // the correct side of it. Entering and closing straight through
                // is not a defence, it is a failure, and that is the branch
                // above.
                bool entered = low <= o.top and high >= o.bottom
                bool reacted = entered and (o.bullish ? close > o.bottom : close < o.top)
                if not flips and entered and o.state < ST_TOUCHED
                    o.state := ST_TOUCHED
                if not flips and reacted
                    o.mitigated := true

    // ---- 2. CREATION on a confirmed structure break -------------------------
    // WHY CHoCH IS EXCLUDED, and why the exclusion is definitional rather than
    // a preference: under the displacement-anchored definition an order block
    // only exists if the leg that left it carried intent. Stage 2 promotes a
    // CHoCH to MSS exactly when its breaking leg contains displacement, so a
    // break that is STILL labelled CHoCH is precisely the reversal break that
    // lacked displacement -- the one case the definition rules out. Admitting
    // CHoCH here would readmit the sloppy "last opposing candle" behaviour by
    // the back door.
    // SELF-CORRECTING: if requireDisplacementForMSS is ever set false, stage 2
    // labels every reversal break MSS and nothing is ever left as CHoCH, so
    // this filter stops excluding anything and order blocks are created on all
    // structure breaks. The input change does the work; no edit needed here.
    bool structNow  = not na(lastStructBar) and lastStructBar == bar_index
    bool structIsBrk = lastStructType == "BOS" or lastStructType == "MSS"
    if structNow and structIsBrk
        bool upBreak = lastStructDir > 0
        // Hunt back for the LAST opposing candle before the leg. k starts at 1
        // so the breaking bar itself is never the anchor: the block has to
        // precede the leg, not be part of it.
        int anchorK = -1
        for k = 1 to obLookbackForAnchor
            if anchorK < 0
                bool opposing = upBreak ? (close[k] < open[k]) : (close[k] > open[k])
                if opposing
                    anchorK := k
        if anchorK >= 0
            float aTop = obUseWholeCandle ? high[anchorK] : math.max(open[anchorK], close[anchorK])
            float aBot = obUseWholeCandle ? low[anchorK]  : math.min(open[anchorK], close[anchorK])
            if aTop > aBot
                bool coiOb = f_obCoincidesWithFvg(aTop, aBot, upBreak)
                if coiOb
                    fvgObCoincidenceCount += 1
                OB o = OB.new(top = aTop, bottom = aBot, bullish = upBreak,
                         anchorBar = bar_index - anchorK, createdBar = bar_index,
                         expiresBar = bar_index + obMaxAgeBars, state = ST_FRESH,
                         mitigated = false, fromMss = lastStructType == "MSS")
                if showOB
                    color oc = upBreak ? colObBull : colObBear
                    o.bx := box.new(bar_index - anchorK, aTop, bar_index + 1, aBot,
                             xloc = xloc.bar_index, extend = extend.right,
                             bgcolor = color.new(oc, 90),
                             border_color = color.new(oc, 30),
                             border_width = 2, border_style = line.style_solid)
                array.push(obs, o)
                cumOb += 1
                f_capObs()

// =============================================================================
// SECTION N (STAGE 3): DEALING RANGE, PREMIUM / DISCOUNT, OTE
// The dealing range is NOT an arbitrary swing-to-swing box. It is defined by
// the setup itself: from the liquidity that was taken (the sweep extreme) to
// where the leg that broke structure ran out (the leg terminus). Everything
// below 50% of that range is discount, everything above is premium, and the
// OTE band is the slice of the retracement where an entry gets paid for the
// move that already happened.
// =============================================================================

var float drLow    = na
var float drHigh   = na
var bool  drIsLong = false
var int   drBar    = na

// Running leg extreme since each side's most recent sweep. This is how we name
// the leg terminus WITHOUT a variable-length ta.highest(), which would have to
// be called unconditionally on every bar to keep its history correct and would
// still be measuring the wrong window whenever a new sweep landed.
var float legHighSinceSellSweep = na
var float legLowSinceBuySweep   = na

// The most recent MSS and the bar its breaking leg started from. Used by the
// POI ranking to prefer zones the MSS leg actually created.
var int lastMssBar      = na
var int lastMssLegStart = na

if barstate.isconfirmed
    Sweep swSell = getLiveSweep(false)
    Sweep swBuy  = getLiveSweep(true)
    bool sellSweepNow = not na(swSell) and swSell.confirmBarIdx == bar_index
    bool buySweepNow  = not na(swBuy)  and swBuy.confirmBarIdx  == bar_index

    if sellSweepNow
        legHighSinceSellSweep := high
    if not sellSweepNow and not na(legHighSinceSellSweep)
        legHighSinceSellSweep := math.max(legHighSinceSellSweep, high)
    if buySweepNow
        legLowSinceBuySweep := low
    if not buySweepNow and not na(legLowSinceBuySweep)
        legLowSinceBuySweep := math.min(legLowSinceBuySweep, low)

    // ---- Define the range when an MSS pairs with a sweep ---------------------
    bool mssNow = not na(lastStructBar) and lastStructBar == bar_index and lastStructType == "MSS"

    if mssNow and lastStructDir > 0
        lastMssBar      := bar_index
        lastMssLegStart := brokenSwingHighBar
    if mssNow and lastStructDir < 0
        lastMssBar      := bar_index
        lastMssLegStart := brokenSwingLowBar

    // LONG setup: sell-side liquidity taken, then a bullish MSS. Range runs
    // from the swept low up to the terminus of the leg that broke structure.
    if mssNow and lastStructDir > 0 and not na(swSell) and swSell.mssConfirmed and not na(legHighSinceSellSweep)
        if legHighSinceSellSweep > swSell.sweepExtreme
            drLow    := swSell.sweepExtreme
            drHigh   := legHighSinceSellSweep
            drIsLong := true
            drBar    := bar_index

    // SHORT setup: mirror.
    if mssNow and lastStructDir < 0 and not na(swBuy) and swBuy.mssConfirmed and not na(legLowSinceBuySweep)
        if swBuy.sweepExtreme > legLowSinceBuySweep
            drHigh   := swBuy.sweepExtreme
            drLow    := legLowSinceBuySweep
            drIsLong := false
            drBar    := bar_index

    // ---- Maintain / kill the range ------------------------------------------
    // A live leg EXTENDS its range: if price keeps making highs on a long
    // setup, the leg is still the leg and the OTE band re-anchors to it. The
    // range only dies when its PREMISE dies -- a close back beyond the swept
    // extreme -- or when it simply gets too old to mean anything.
    if not na(drLow) and not na(drHigh) and not na(drBar)
        bool drDead = bar_index - drBar > drMaxAgeBars
        if drIsLong and close < drLow
            drDead := true
        if not drIsLong and close > drHigh
            drDead := true
        if not drDead and drIsLong
            drHigh := math.max(drHigh, high)
        if not drDead and not drIsLong
            drLow := math.min(drLow, low)
        if drDead
            drLow  := na
            drHigh := na
            drBar  := na

// ---- Derived levels, recomputed every bar from confirmed state --------------
// These sit OUTSIDE the confirmed block on purpose: they are pure functions of
// drLow/drHigh, which only ever change on a confirmed bar, so reading them on
// the live bar returns the last confirmed geometry rather than something that
// moves intrabar.
float drRange = na(drLow) or na(drHigh) ? na : drHigh - drLow
float drEq    = na(drRange) ? na : (drHigh + drLow) / 2

// OTE band for a LONG: a retracement DOWN from the leg high, so oteHigh (0.79)
// gives the LOWER price. For a SHORT: a retracement UP from the leg low.
float oteLongLo  = na(drRange) ? na : drHigh - drRange * oteHigh
float oteLongHi  = na(drRange) ? na : drHigh - drRange * oteLow
float oteShortLo = na(drRange) ? na : drLow  + drRange * oteLow
float oteShortHi = na(drRange) ? na : drLow  + drRange * oteHigh

// The classic 0.705 sweet spot, drawn for whichever direction the range is.
float ote62  = na(drRange) ? na : (drIsLong ? drHigh - drRange * oteLow  : drLow + drRange * oteLow)
float ote705 = na(drRange) ? na : (drIsLong ? drHigh - drRange * 0.705   : drLow + drRange * 0.705)
float ote79  = na(drRange) ? na : (drIsLong ? drHigh - drRange * oteHigh : drLow + drRange * oteHigh)

// ---- PUBLIC accessors -------------------------------------------------------
// drLow / drHigh are na when no range is defined; the booleans return false
// rather than na, because "no range" must never read as a permissive signal.
hasDealingRange() =>
    bool r = not na(drLow) and not na(drHigh)
    r

inDiscount() =>
    bool r = false
    if not na(drEq)
        r := close < drEq
    r

inPremium() =>
    bool r = false
    if not na(drEq)
        r := close > drEq
    r

inOTE(bool isLong) =>
    bool r = false
    if not na(drRange)
        float lo = isLong ? oteLongLo : oteShortLo
        float hi = isLong ? oteLongHi : oteShortHi
        r := close >= lo and close <= hi
        if oteRequireCorrectSide and isLong
            r := r and close < drEq
        if oteRequireCorrectSide and not isLong
            r := r and close > drEq
    r

// =============================================================================
// SECTION O (STAGE 3): THE UNIFIED POI API
//
// WHY THIS EXISTS: a displacement leg that breaks structure normally leaves an
// order block AND a fair value gap, anchored to adjacent candles, covering
// almost the same prices. They are not two independent confirmations. They are
// one event observed twice. Stage 5 therefore gets ONE query -- bestPOI() --
// worth ONE component, and the overlap is expressed as a QUALITY BONUS rather
// than a second score line.
//
// ELIGIBILITY (what counts as unmitigated):
//   FVG / IFVG : state FRESH or TOUCHED. A CE tag is the gap's mitigation --
//                you do not enter at a level price has already visited and left.
//   OB         : state up to CE_TAGGED and not yet mitigated.
//   BREAKER    : state BREAKER, polarity INVERTED from the original block.
// =============================================================================

// Does this zone intersect the OTE band for its own direction?
f_zoneInOte(float top, float bottom, bool bullish) =>
    bool r = false
    float lo = bullish ? oteLongLo : oteShortLo
    float hi = bullish ? oteLongHi : oteShortHi
    if not na(lo) and not na(hi)
        r := bottom <= hi and top >= lo
    r

// Was this zone created by the displacement leg of the most recent MSS?
f_fromMssLeg(int srcBar) =>
    bool r = false
    if not na(lastMssBar) and not na(lastMssLegStart)
        r := srcBar >= lastMssLegStart and srcBar <= lastMssBar + MSS_LEG_GRACE_BARS
    r

// --- QUALITY, 0.40 to 1.00 ---------------------------------------------------
// base       0.40  A valid, unmitigated, correctly-polarised zone is real
//                  evidence on its own. Stage 5's 2-point POI component must
//                  not collapse to zero just because the location is ordinary.
// + OTE      0.25  The largest bonus, because WHERE the zone sits is the
//                  strongest independent filter available: a long POI sitting
//                  in premium is a worse entry no matter how it was formed.
// + MSS leg  0.20  Provenance. A zone left by the leg that actually broke
//                  structure is where the initiating orders sat. Weighted
//                  below OTE because it is partly correlated with it -- MSS-leg
//                  zones often land in the OTE band anyway -- and correlated
//                  evidence must not stack at full weight.
// + overlap  0.15  The SMALLEST bonus, deliberately. FVG/OB coincidence is the
//                  most collinear of the three: both are products of the same
//                  displacement leg. It is confirming, so it earns something,
//                  but treating it as a full extra factor would reintroduce the
//                  double-count this whole section exists to prevent.
f_poiQuality(bool inOte, bool fromMss, bool coincident) =>
    float q = 0.40
    if inOte
        q += 0.25
    if fromMss
        q += 0.20
    if coincident
        q += 0.15
    q

// --- Rebuild the book on every confirmed bar ---------------------------------
// Rebuilt rather than incrementally maintained because quality depends on the
// OTE band and the current MSS leg, both of which move. Rebuilding on confirmed
// bars only means a live-bar query returns the last confirmed book, which is
// exactly the anti-repaint behaviour we want.
if barstate.isconfirmed
    array.clear(poiBook)

    if array.size(fvgs) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(fvgs) - 1
            FVG g = array.get(fvgs, i)
            if g.state <= ST_TOUCHED
                bool ote = f_zoneInOte(g.top, g.bottom, g.bullish)
                bool mss = f_fromMssLeg(g.createdBar)
                bool coi = f_fvgCoincidesWithOb(g.top, g.bottom, g.bullish)
                array.push(poiBook, POI.new(top = g.top, bottom = g.bottom, ce = g.ce,
                         bullish = g.bullish, kind = "FVG",
                         quality = f_poiQuality(ote, mss, coi), sourceBar = g.createdBar,
                         inOte = ote, fromMssLeg = mss))

    if array.size(ifvgs) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(ifvgs) - 1
            IFVG iv = array.get(ifvgs, i)
            if iv.state <= ST_TOUCHED
                bool oteI = f_zoneInOte(iv.top, iv.bottom, iv.bullish)
                bool mssI = f_fromMssLeg(iv.createdBar)
                bool coiI = f_fvgCoincidesWithOb(iv.top, iv.bottom, iv.bullish)
                array.push(poiBook, POI.new(top = iv.top, bottom = iv.bottom, ce = iv.ce,
                         bullish = iv.bullish, kind = "IFVG",
                         quality = f_poiQuality(oteI, mssI, coiI), sourceBar = iv.createdBar,
                         inOte = oteI, fromMssLeg = mssI))

    if array.size(obs) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(obs) - 1
            OB o = array.get(obs, i)
            float oCe = (o.top + o.bottom) / 2
            // Live block, original polarity.
            if o.state <= ST_CE_TAGGED and not o.mitigated
                bool oteO = f_zoneInOte(o.top, o.bottom, o.bullish)
                bool mssO = o.fromMss or f_fromMssLeg(o.anchorBar)
                bool coiO = f_obCoincidesWithFvg(o.top, o.bottom, o.bullish)
                array.push(poiBook, POI.new(top = o.top, bottom = o.bottom, ce = oCe,
                         bullish = o.bullish, kind = "OB",
                         quality = f_poiQuality(oteO, mssO, coiO), sourceBar = o.anchorBar,
                         inOte = oteO, fromMssLeg = mssO))
            // Failed block, INVERTED polarity.
            if o.state == ST_BREAKER
                bool bkBull = not o.bullish
                bool oteB = f_zoneInOte(o.top, o.bottom, bkBull)
                bool mssB = f_fromMssLeg(o.anchorBar)
                bool coiB = f_obCoincidesWithFvg(o.top, o.bottom, bkBull)
                array.push(poiBook, POI.new(top = o.top, bottom = o.bottom, ce = oCe,
                         bullish = bkBull, kind = "BREAKER",
                         quality = f_poiQuality(oteB, mssB, coiB), sourceBar = o.anchorBar,
                         inOte = oteB, fromMssLeg = mssB))

// --- PUBLIC: the single query stage 5 makes ----------------------------------
// Ranking is strictly lexicographic, matching the stated order:
//   1. polarity + eligibility  (already applied when the book was built)
//   2. intersects the OTE band
//   3. created by the most recent MSS leg
//   4. nearest to px
// rank = 2*inOte + 1*fromMssLeg reproduces 2-then-3 exactly, because an OTE
// hit alone (2) outranks an MSS-leg hit alone (1).
bestPOI(bool isLong, float px) =>
    POI best = na
    if array.size(poiBook) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(poiBook) - 1
            POI c = array.get(poiBook, i)
            if c.bullish == isLong
                if na(best)
                    best := c
                if not na(best)
                    int cRank = (c.inOte ? 2 : 0) + (c.fromMssLeg ? 1 : 0)
                    int bRank = (best.inOte ? 2 : 0) + (best.fromMssLeg ? 1 : 0)
                    bool better = false
                    if cRank > bRank
                        better := true
                    if cRank == bRank and math.abs(c.ce - px) < math.abs(best.ce - px)
                        better := true
                    if better
                        best := c
    best

// =============================================================================
// SECTION P (STAGE 3): OTE VISUALS
// The band is maintained on CONFIRMED bars, not just on the last bar, so that
// a range which lived and died in the middle of history can still be frozen at
// the bar it actually died on. An islast-only version could never do that,
// because islast never runs on those bars.
// Live cost is fixed: one box and three lines, reused. extend.right means the
// right edge never needs touching while the band is alive.
// =============================================================================

var box  oteBx    = na
var line oteLn62  = na
var line oteLn705 = na
var line oteLn79  = na

// Archive of dead bands, only populated when showHistoricalOTE is on.
var array<box>  oteHistBx = array.new<box>()
var array<line> oteHistLn = array.new<line>()

f_archiveOteBand(box b, line l1, line l2, line l3) =>
    array.push(oteHistBx, b)
    array.push(oteHistLn, l1)
    array.push(oteHistLn, l2)
    array.push(oteHistLn, l3)
    while array.size(oteHistBx) > MAX_OTE_HIST
        box.delete(array.shift(oteHistBx))
        line.delete(array.shift(oteHistLn))
        line.delete(array.shift(oteHistLn))
        line.delete(array.shift(oteHistLn))

if barstate.isconfirmed
    bool oteLive = showOTE and not na(drRange) and not na(drBar)

    if oteLive
        float bandLo = drIsLong ? oteLongLo : oteShortLo
        float bandHi = drIsLong ? oteLongHi : oteShortHi
        if na(oteBx)
            oteBx := box.new(drBar, bandHi, bar_index, bandLo, xloc = xloc.bar_index,
                     extend = extend.right, bgcolor = color.new(colOte, 90),
                     border_color = color.new(colOte, 45), border_width = 1,
                     border_style = line.style_dashed)
            oteLn62  := line.new(drBar, ote62,  bar_index, ote62,  xloc = xloc.bar_index,
                     extend = extend.right, color = color.new(colOte, 55), style = line.style_dotted)
            oteLn705 := line.new(drBar, ote705, bar_index, ote705, xloc = xloc.bar_index,
                     extend = extend.right, color = color.new(colOte, 15), style = line.style_solid)
            oteLn79  := line.new(drBar, ote79,  bar_index, ote79,  xloc = xloc.bar_index,
                     extend = extend.right, color = color.new(colOte, 55), style = line.style_dotted)
        if not na(oteBx)
            // The band re-anchors as the leg extends, so top/bottom move.
            box.set_left(oteBx, drBar)
            box.set_top(oteBx, bandHi)
            box.set_bottom(oteBx, bandLo)
            line.set_xy1(oteLn62,  drBar, ote62)
            line.set_xy2(oteLn62,  bar_index, ote62)
            line.set_xy1(oteLn705, drBar, ote705)
            line.set_xy2(oteLn705, bar_index, ote705)
            line.set_xy1(oteLn79,  drBar, ote79)
            line.set_xy2(oteLn79,  bar_index, ote79)

    // The range died. Either archive the band frozen at this bar, or drop it.
    if not oteLive and not na(oteBx)
        if showHistoricalOTE
            box.set_extend(oteBx, extend.none)
            box.set_right(oteBx, bar_index)
            box.set_bgcolor(oteBx, color.new(colDead, 92))
            box.set_border_color(oteBx, color.new(colDead, 60))
            line.set_extend(oteLn62,  extend.none)
            line.set_extend(oteLn705, extend.none)
            line.set_extend(oteLn79,  extend.none)
            line.set_x2(oteLn62,  bar_index)
            line.set_x2(oteLn705, bar_index)
            line.set_x2(oteLn79,  bar_index)
            line.set_color(oteLn62,  color.new(colDead, 75))
            line.set_color(oteLn705, color.new(colDead, 55))
            line.set_color(oteLn79,  color.new(colDead, 75))
            f_archiveOteBand(oteBx, oteLn62, oteLn705, oteLn79)
        if not showHistoricalOTE
            box.delete(oteBx)
            line.delete(oteLn62)
            line.delete(oteLn705)
            line.delete(oteLn79)
        oteBx    := na
        oteLn62  := na
        oteLn705 := na
        oteLn79  := na

// =============================================================================
// SECTION Q (STAGE 4): SMT DIVERGENCE (MNQ vs ES)
//
// SMT is the observation that two instruments which normally move together
// stopped agreeing at a level: NQ takes out its high while ES cannot. That is
// evidence the push was one index running stops rather than the market bidding.
//
// IT IS CONFLUENCE ONLY. Nothing in this section arms a setup, sets a bias, or
// touches sweep / structure / POI state. It publishes two read-only values and
// stage 5 weights them at one point.
// =============================================================================

// WHY [1] AND lookahead_off, on a SAME-TIMEFRAME request:
//   lookahead_off alone stops TradingView handing historical bars a value the
//   reference had not published yet. The [1] then guarantees we are reading a
//   reference bar that has CLOSED, which matters because the debug table reads
//   these on the live bar -- without the offset the value would move intrabar
//   and the "is the feed alive" row would be lying about what the logic saw.
//   The cost is that we compare our bar N against the reference's bar N-1. Over
//   a 20-bar swing-structure comparison that one-bar skew is immaterial; the
//   guarantee is not.
// WHY ignore_invalid_symbol:
//   ES and NQ share a session, but the reference can still return na -- the
//   17:00-18:00 ET maintenance break, a holiday, a contract roll gap, or simply
//   a mistyped symbol. Without this flag a bad symbol is a hard script error.
//   With it, every na is handled below as "no opinion", never as "the reference
//   failed to make a higher high", which would manufacture divergences out of
//   missing data.
[refHigh, refLow, refClose] = request.security(smtSymbol, timeframe.period,
     [high[1], low[1], close[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off,
     ignore_invalid_symbol = true)

var int   smtLastBar      = na
var int   smtLastDir      = 0     // +1 bullish (at lows), -1 bearish (at highs)
var float smtLastPx       = na
var float smtLastStrength = 0.0
var int   smtCount        = 0

// ---- TEMPORARY DIAGNOSTICS for the pool-gate investigation ------------------
// smtCandidates counts structural divergences found BEFORE the pool gate is
// applied; smtCount counts those that survived it. If the two are equal the
// gate is not filtering anything.
var int   smtCandidates       = 0
var float smtLastDistAny      = na   // ticks to nearest pool of ANY tier
var float smtLastDistSig      = na   // ticks to nearest pool of tier <= 1
var float smtLastDistProt     = na   // ticks to nearest PROTECTED pool (tier 0)

// Per-bar marker price, reset every bar.
float smtMarkPx = na

// --- reference extreme in a window AROUND a given bar offset ----------------
// The two feeds do not print their extremes on the same bar, so comparing a
// single reference bar against an MNQ pivot would be brittle. A +/- halfWin
// window absorbs that skew. na values are SKIPPED, never treated as extremes.
f_refHighAround(int barsBack, int halfWin) =>
    float m = na
    for k = barsBack - halfWin to barsBack + halfWin
        if k >= 0
            float v = refHigh[k]
            if not na(v) and (na(m) or v > m)
                m := v
    m

f_refLowAround(int barsBack, int halfWin) =>
    float m = na
    for k = barsBack - halfWin to barsBack + halfWin
        if k >= 0
            float v = refLow[k]
            if not na(v) and (na(m) or v < m)
                m := v
    m

// --- reference range over the lookback, na-safe ------------------------------
// Used to normalise the divergence gap. Normalising by the REFERENCE's own
// range is essential: NQ moves roughly three to four times ES in points, so an
// absolute gap would be meaningless across the pair.
f_refRange(int lb) =>
    float hi = na
    float lo = na
    for k = 0 to lb - 1
        float hv = refHigh[k]
        float lv = refLow[k]
        if not na(hv) and (na(hi) or hv > hi)
            hi := hv
        if not na(lv) and (na(lo) or lv < lo)
            lo := lv
    float r = na(hi) or na(lo) ? na : hi - lo
    r

// --- is this extreme sitting on a mapped pool? ------------------------------
// Deliberately does NOT require pool.active. The highest-value SMT is the one
// that prints exactly as a level is swept, and by that bar stage 2 has already
// marked the pool consumed. Requiring active would filter out the best cases.
// Resolve the SMT significance filter. Deliberately its own input rather than a
// reuse of sweepMaxTier: the two answer different questions and one must not
// move when the other does.
int smtMaxTier = switch smtMinTier
    "Protected only"    => TIER_PROTECTED
    "Protected + Equal" => TIER_SIGNIFICANT
    => TIER_TRANSIENT

// Distance in TICKS from `price` to the nearest same-side pool at or below
// `maxTier`. Diagnostic only. Read at THREE tier bands side by side, this is
// what distinguishes a gate matching a meaningful level from one matching
// something trivially co-located with the pivot being tested.
f_nearestPoolDistTicks(float price, bool buySide, int maxTier) =>
    float best = na
    if array.size(pools) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(pools) - 1
            Pool p = array.get(pools, i)
            if p.buySide == buySide and p.tier <= maxTier
                float d = math.abs(p.price - price)
                if na(best) or d < best
                    best := d
    float t = na
    if not na(best)
        t := best / syminfo.mintick
    t

// --- is this extreme sitting on a SIGNIFICANT mapped pool? -------------------
// The maxTier argument is not decoration, it IS the gate.
// WHY: stage 1's pool population runs earlier in the same confirmed bar and
// registers every newly confirmed pivot as a TIER_TRANSIENT pool at exactly
// that pivot's price. Without a tier filter this function was handed the pivot
// and found the pool made from that same pivot, distance 0.0, so `atPool` was
// structurally always true and smtRequireAtPool gated nothing at all. Excluding
// tier 2 removes the self-reference by construction, with no bar-index
// bookkeeping to rot. It is also the right rule on its own terms: "divergence
// at a liquidity pool" has to mean a level that matters, and "this pivot high
// is near a swing high" is true of every pivot by definition.
//
// Still deliberately does NOT require pool.active. The highest-value SMT is the
// one that prints exactly as a level is swept, and by that bar stage 2 has
// already marked the pool consumed. Requiring active would filter out the best
// cases, and it was never the source of the fault.
f_anyPoolNear(float price, float tol, bool buySide, int maxTier) =>
    bool r = false
    if array.size(pools) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(pools) - 1
            Pool p = array.get(pools, i)
            if not r and p.buySide == buySide and p.tier <= maxTier and math.abs(p.price - price) <= tol
                r := true
    r

if barstate.isconfirmed and smtEnabled
    float poolTol = smtPoolProxTicks * syminfo.mintick

    // ---- BEARISH SMT: MNQ higher high, reference fails to follow ------------
    // Triggered only when a NEW MNQ pivot high CONFIRMS, and compared against
    // the PREVIOUS confirmed pivot high. Using two confirmed pivots is what
    // stops a single spiky bar from manufacturing a divergence -- neither side
    // of the comparison is a raw bar high.
    if not na(ph) and array.size(swingHighPrices) >= 2
        int   nH      = array.size(swingHighPrices)
        float mnqCur  = array.get(swingHighPrices, nH - 1)
        float mnqPrev = array.get(swingHighPrices, nH - 2)
        int   curBar  = array.get(swingHighBars,   nH - 1)
        int   prevBar = array.get(swingHighBars,   nH - 2)

        bool inWindow = (curBar - prevBar) <= smtLookbackBars and (bar_index - prevBar) <= smtLookbackBars + 2 * pivotLen
        if mnqCur > mnqPrev and inWindow
            float refCur  = f_refHighAround(bar_index - curBar,  pivotLen)
            float refPrev = f_refHighAround(bar_index - prevBar, pivotLen)
            // Both must be real numbers. A missing reference is "no opinion".
            if not na(refCur) and not na(refPrev) and refCur <= refPrev
                smtCandidates += 1
                smtLastDistAny  := f_nearestPoolDistTicks(mnqCur, true, TIER_TRANSIENT)
                smtLastDistSig  := f_nearestPoolDistTicks(mnqCur, true, TIER_SIGNIFICANT)
                smtLastDistProt := f_nearestPoolDistTicks(mnqCur, true, TIER_PROTECTED)
                bool atPool = f_anyPoolNear(mnqCur, poolTol, true, smtMaxTier)
                if atPool or not smtRequireAtPool
                    float rr   = f_refRange(smtLookbackBars)
                    float frac = na(rr) or rr <= 0 ? 0.0 : math.min((refPrev - refCur) / rr, 1.0)
                    smtLastStrength := 0.5 + 0.3 * frac + (atPool ? 0.2 : 0.0)
                    smtLastDir      := -1
                    smtLastBar      := bar_index
                    smtLastPx       := mnqCur
                    smtMarkPx       := mnqCur
                    smtCount        += 1
                    if showSMT
                        f_pushS2Label(label.new(curBar, mnqCur,
                                 "SMT " + str.tostring(smtLastStrength, "#.00"),
                                 xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_down,
                                 color = color.new(colSmt, 80), textcolor = color.new(colSmt, 0),
                                 size = size.tiny))

    // ---- BULLISH SMT: MNQ lower low, reference refuses to follow ------------
    if not na(pl) and array.size(swingLowPrices) >= 2
        int   nL       = array.size(swingLowPrices)
        float mnqCurL  = array.get(swingLowPrices, nL - 1)
        float mnqPrevL = array.get(swingLowPrices, nL - 2)
        int   curBarL  = array.get(swingLowBars,   nL - 1)
        int   prevBarL = array.get(swingLowBars,   nL - 2)

        bool inWindowL = (curBarL - prevBarL) <= smtLookbackBars and (bar_index - prevBarL) <= smtLookbackBars + 2 * pivotLen
        if mnqCurL < mnqPrevL and inWindowL
            float refCurL  = f_refLowAround(bar_index - curBarL,  pivotLen)
            float refPrevL = f_refLowAround(bar_index - prevBarL, pivotLen)
            if not na(refCurL) and not na(refPrevL) and refCurL >= refPrevL
                smtCandidates += 1
                smtLastDistAny  := f_nearestPoolDistTicks(mnqCurL, false, TIER_TRANSIENT)
                smtLastDistSig  := f_nearestPoolDistTicks(mnqCurL, false, TIER_SIGNIFICANT)
                smtLastDistProt := f_nearestPoolDistTicks(mnqCurL, false, TIER_PROTECTED)
                bool atPoolL = f_anyPoolNear(mnqCurL, poolTol, false, smtMaxTier)
                if atPoolL or not smtRequireAtPool
                    float rrL   = f_refRange(smtLookbackBars)
                    float fracL = na(rrL) or rrL <= 0 ? 0.0 : math.min((refCurL - refPrevL) / rrL, 1.0)
                    smtLastStrength := 0.5 + 0.3 * fracL + (atPoolL ? 0.2 : 0.0)
                    smtLastDir      := 1
                    smtLastBar      := bar_index
                    smtLastPx       := mnqCurL
                    smtMarkPx       := mnqCurL
                    smtCount        += 1
                    if showSMT
                        f_pushS2Label(label.new(curBarL, mnqCurL,
                                 "SMT " + str.tostring(smtLastStrength, "#.00"),
                                 xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_up,
                                 color = color.new(colSmt, 80), textcolor = color.new(colSmt, 0),
                                 size = size.tiny))

// --- PUBLIC: is a divergence live on this side? -----------------------------
// A divergence goes stale after smtLookbackBars. Reusing that input rather than
// adding a validity knob keeps one number describing one idea: how far back
// swing structure is still comparable.
smtDivergence(bool bullish) =>
    bool r = false
    if smtEnabled and not na(smtLastBar) and bar_index - smtLastBar <= smtLookbackBars
        r := bullish ? smtLastDir > 0 : smtLastDir < 0
    r

// --- PUBLIC: graded strength, 0 to 1 ----------------------------------------
// GRADED RATHER THAN BOOLEAN, on purpose. A divergence where ES prints a
// decisively lower high is a different observation from one where it prints a
// high a tick short of its last -- the second is inside the noise of an
// overnight book. A boolean scores those identically; stage 5 multiplying its
// 1 point by this does not.
//   0.5  base, a confirmed two-pivot divergence
// + 0.3  scaled by how far the reference fell short, as a fraction of the
//        reference's own lookback range
// + 0.2  the divergent extreme sits on a mapped pool
smtStrengthNow() =>
    float v = 0.0
    if smtEnabled and not na(smtLastBar) and bar_index - smtLastBar <= smtLookbackBars
        v := smtLastStrength
    v

// --- Visuals -----------------------------------------------------------------
// A diamond, not the sweep's cross, and indigo rather than the red/teal pool
// palette, so an SMT can never be mistaken for a sweep at a glance.
plotshape(showSMT and smtEnabled ? smtMarkPx : na, title = "SMT divergence",
     style = shape.diamond, location = location.absolute,
     color = color.new(colSmt, 0), size = size.tiny)

// =============================================================================
// SECTION R (STAGE 5): CONFLUENCE SCORING
//
// Six components, ten points. Two of them are MANDATORY and gate everything
// else: without a liquidity sweep AND an MSS confirming that same sweep, the
// score is zero regardless of how much peripheral evidence is present.
// Peripheral points must never be able to arm a setup on their own.
//
// The threshold is 7.0 and the mandatory pair plus the POI component tops out
// at 3.0 + 2.0 + 1.5 = 6.5. That gap is deliberate: it makes confluence
// load-bearing even in the best-formed setups, rather than decorative.
//
// COLLINEARITY: the two location components deliberately measure DIFFERENT
// ranges. The dealing-range component asks where price sits inside the setup's
// own range; the session component asks where it sits inside the session or
// prior day. Price can be in dealing-range discount and session premium at the
// same time. If they measured the same range they would be one fact with two
// names, which is the failure this whole model is built to avoid.
// =============================================================================

type Score
    bool   isLong
    bool   gateOk
    float  sweepPts
    float  mssPts
    float  poiPts
    float  locPts
    float  smtPts
    float  sessPts
    float  total
    bool   pass
    bool   strong
    string poolTag
    int    poolTier
    string poiKind

// ---- A. SESSION PREMIUM / DISCOUNT (the reserved point, now live) ------------
// Reference range, per the rangeRef input.
f_sessRefHi() =>
    float v = na
    if rangeRef == "Prior day RTH"
        v := pdhRth
    if rangeRef == "Prior day full"
        v := pdhFull
    if rangeRef == "Current session"
        // Whichever session range stage 1 is currently building. RTH is
        // included: without it every RTH setup would take a systematic
        // one-point penalty for a reason that has nothing to do with the setup.
        v := inAsiaRaw ? asiaCurHigh : inLondonRaw ? lonCurHigh : inRthRaw ? rthCurHigh : na
    v

f_sessRefLo() =>
    float v = na
    if rangeRef == "Prior day RTH"
        v := pdlRth
    if rangeRef == "Prior day full"
        v := pdlFull
    if rangeRef == "Current session"
        v := inAsiaRaw ? asiaCurLow : inLondonRaw ? lonCurLow : inRthRaw ? rthCurLow : na
    v

// Graded, not binary: 0 wrong side, 0.5 correct side, 1.0 beyond sessionPdDepth.
// RETURNS 0 CLEANLY when the reference range is undefined or too small to mean
// anything. EARLY ASIA IS THEREFORE STRUCTURALLY HARDER TO FIRE, and that is
// intended rather than a defect: in the first bars of a session there is no
// established range, so there is genuinely no premium/discount fact to report.
// Abstaining is the honest answer; guessing from a three-point range would let
// two ticks flip the reading from deep discount to deep premium.
f_sessionPdGrade(bool isLong) =>
    float g  = 0.0
    float hi = f_sessRefHi()
    float lo = f_sessRefLo()
    if not na(hi) and not na(lo) and hi > lo
        float span = hi - lo
        if na(atr) or span >= SESS_PD_MIN_RANGE_ATR * atr
            float frac  = (close - lo) / span
            float depth = isLong ? frac : 1.0 - frac
            if depth < 0.5
                g := 0.50
            if depth <= sessionPdDepth
                g := 1.00
    g

// ---- Dealing-range location grade -------------------------------------------
// 0 wrong side of equilibrium, 0.5 correct side outside OTE, 1.0 inside OTE.
// inOTE() already applies oteRequireCorrectSide, so the 1.0 grade cannot be
// reached on the wrong side of the range.
f_locationGrade(bool isLong) =>
    float g = 0.0
    if not na(drRange) and drRange > 0 and not na(drEq)
        bool correctSide = isLong ? close < drEq : close > drEq
        if correctSide
            g := 0.50
        if inOTE(isLong)
            g := 1.00
    g

// ---- B. THE MODEL -----------------------------------------------------------
f_computeScore(bool isLong) =>
    // A LONG setup is built on SELL-side liquidity being taken, so we ask for
    // the sweep on the opposite side to the trade direction.
    Sweep sw = getLiveSweep(not isLong)

    // THE MANDATORY GATE. Both halves required: a live sweep, and an MSS that
    // stage 2 actually paired with THAT sweep.
    bool gate = false
    if not na(sw)
        gate := sw.mssConfirmed

    float sweepPts = 0.0
    float mssPts   = 0.0
    float poiPts   = 0.0
    float locPts   = 0.0
    float smtPts   = 0.0
    float sessPts  = 0.0
    string pTag    = "-"
    int    pTier   = -1
    string pKind   = "none"

    if gate
        // 1. Sweep, scaled by how significant the level taken was.
        sweepPts := wSweep * poolWeight(sw.poolTier)
        pTag  := sw.poolTag
        pTier := sw.poolTier

        // 2. MSS. Binary, and given the gate it always contributes in full --
        //    it is a floor, not a discriminator. Worth remembering when reading
        //    the per-component breakdown.
        mssPts := wMss

        // 3. The single POI component. One query, one component: an order block
        //    and an FVG from the same leg are one observation, not two.
        POI p = bestPOI(isLong, close)
        if not na(p)
            poiPts := wPoi * p.quality
            pKind  := p.kind

        // 4. Where price sits inside the SETUP's own range.
        locPts := wLocation * f_locationGrade(isLong)

        // 5. SMT, graded by strength and halved during Asia. A bullish SMT (at
        //    lows) supports a long, so the direction argument matches isLong.
        if smtDivergence(isLong)
            smtPts := wSmt * smtStrengthNow() * (inAsia ? SMT_ASIA_SCALE : 1.0)

        // 6. Where price sits inside the SESSION or prior day. Different range,
        //    so not collinear with component 4.
        sessPts := wSessionPd * f_sessionPdGrade(isLong)

    float total = sweepPts + mssPts + poiPts + locPts + smtPts + sessPts
    Score sc = Score.new(isLong = isLong, gateOk = gate,
             sweepPts = sweepPts, mssPts = mssPts, poiPts = poiPts,
             locPts = locPts, smtPts = smtPts, sessPts = sessPts,
             total = total, pass = gate and total >= scoreThreshold,
             strong = gate and total >= scoreStrongBand,
             poolTag = pTag, poolTier = pTier, poiKind = pKind)
    sc

// ---- Cached scores, recomputed on confirmed bars only ------------------------
// The table and stage 6 read the cache, so a live-bar read returns the last
// CONFIRMED score rather than something that moves intrabar.
var Score scLong  = na
var Score scShort = na

// ---- Score distribution, one sample per ARMED SETUP -------------------------
// Buckets: <5, 5-6, 6-7, 7-8, 8+.
// SAMPLING CHOICE: we record the PEAK score a setup ever reached, once, when
// the setup ends. Sampling every bar would let one long-lived sweep dominate
// the histogram. Sampling at arm time would systematically understate the
// location components, because on the MSS bar price is at the leg extreme and
// has not retraced into OTE yet. The peak is what the setup was worth at its
// best, which is the number a trader would actually have acted on.
var array<int> scoreBuckets = array.new<int>(5, 0)

f_bucketScore(float v) =>
    int idx = v < 5.0 ? 0 : v < 6.0 ? 1 : v < 7.0 ? 2 : v < 8.0 ? 3 : 4
    array.set(scoreBuckets, idx, array.get(scoreBuckets, idx) + 1)

var float peakLong    = na
var int   peakSwLong  = na
var float peakShort   = na
var int   peakSwShort = na

// How many armed setups EVER had a live dealing range while armed. If this
// fraction is low, both location components are structurally dead and the max
// achievable score drops by 3.0 points.
var int  armedSetups   = 0
var int  armedWithDR   = 0
var bool curHadDrLong  = false
var bool curHadDrShort = false

if barstate.isconfirmed
    scLong  := f_computeScore(true)
    scShort := f_computeScore(false)

    // --- LONG side peak tracking ---
    Sweep swL = getLiveSweep(false)
    bool gateL = not na(swL) and scLong.gateOk
    if gateL and (na(peakSwLong) or peakSwLong != swL.confirmBarIdx)
        // A different setup than the one being tracked: bank the old peak.
        if not na(peakLong)
            f_bucketScore(peakLong)
            armedSetups += 1
            if curHadDrLong
                armedWithDR += 1
        peakSwLong    := swL.confirmBarIdx
        peakLong      := scLong.total
        curHadDrLong  := false
    if gateL and not na(peakSwLong) and peakSwLong == swL.confirmBarIdx
        peakLong := math.max(nz(peakLong, 0.0), scLong.total)
        if hasDealingRange()
            curHadDrLong := true
    if not gateL and not na(peakLong)
        f_bucketScore(peakLong)
        armedSetups += 1
        if curHadDrLong
            armedWithDR += 1
        peakLong     := na
        peakSwLong   := na
        curHadDrLong := false

    // --- SHORT side peak tracking ---
    Sweep swS = getLiveSweep(true)
    bool gateS = not na(swS) and scShort.gateOk
    if gateS and (na(peakSwShort) or peakSwShort != swS.confirmBarIdx)
        if not na(peakShort)
            f_bucketScore(peakShort)
            armedSetups += 1
            if curHadDrShort
                armedWithDR += 1
        peakSwShort   := swS.confirmBarIdx
        peakShort     := scShort.total
        curHadDrShort := false
    if gateS and not na(peakSwShort) and peakSwShort == swS.confirmBarIdx
        peakShort := math.max(nz(peakShort, 0.0), scShort.total)
        if hasDealingRange()
            curHadDrShort := true
    if not gateS and not na(peakShort)
        f_bucketScore(peakShort)
        armedSetups += 1
        if curHadDrShort
            armedWithDR += 1
        peakShort     := na
        peakSwShort   := na
        curHadDrShort := false

// ---- C. PUBLIC OUTPUT --------------------------------------------------------
// scoreFor() is the real interface: stage 6 and validation both need to know
// WHY a number came out the way it did, not merely what it was.
scoreFor(bool isLong) =>
    Score sc = isLong ? scLong : scShort
    sc

currentScore(bool isLong) =>
    Score sc = isLong ? scLong : scShort
    float v = 0.0
    if not na(sc)
        v := sc.total
    v

scorePasses(bool isLong) =>
    Score sc = isLong ? scLong : scShort
    bool r = false
    if not na(sc)
        r := sc.pass
    r

// =============================================================================
// SECTION S (STAGE 6): ENTRY TRIGGER, GUARD RAILS, SIZING, ALERTS
//
// THIS IS AN INDICATOR. Nothing below places an order. It maintains a VIRTUAL
// position so that TP1, stop and runner alerts can fire, and it reports what a
// trade WOULD have been. Every number is display and alert payload.
//
// GUARD RAIL COUNTING PRINCIPLE: a counter increments when a guard blocks a
// would-be TRIGGER, not on every bar the guard happens to be true. Counting
// per bar would let one long-lived condition swamp the breakdown and tell you
// nothing about which rail is actually doing work. The two exceptions are the
// spent debounce and the ambiguity guard, which are counted once per episode
// for the same reason.
// =============================================================================

// ---- Buffer resolution, same three-mode shape as everywhere else ------------
f_stopBuffer() =>
    float tTicks = stopBufferTicks * syminfo.mintick
    float tAtr   = stopBufferAtrMult * nz(atr)
    float res    = switch stopBufferMode
        "Ticks" => tTicks
        "ATR"   => tAtr
        => math.max(tTicks, tAtr)
    res

// ---- Session windows, DST-safe via time() -----------------------------------
bool pastAsiaCutoff   = not na(time(timeframe.period, asiaCutoff,    TZ))
bool pastLondonCutoff = not na(time(timeframe.period, londonCutoff,  TZ))
bool inAsiaFlatten    = not na(time(timeframe.period, asiaFlatten,   TZ))
bool inLondonFlatten  = not na(time(timeframe.period, londonFlatten, TZ))
bool pastCutoff  = (inAsiaRaw and pastAsiaCutoff) or (inLondonRaw and pastLondonCutoff)
bool flattenNow  = (inAsiaRaw and inAsiaFlatten)  or (inLondonRaw and inLondonFlatten)

// ---- Virtual position state -------------------------------------------------
var int    posDir      = 0        // 0 flat, +1 long, -1 short
var float  posEntry    = na
var float  posStop     = na
var float  posTp1      = na
var float  posRunner   = na
var bool   posTp1Hit   = false
var int    posBar      = na
var int    posQty      = 0

// ---- Last signal, for the table and for the min-bars guard -------------------
var int    lastSigDir     = 0
var float  lastSigScore   = na    // score AT TRIGGER
var float  lastSigPeak    = na    // peak the setup reached, a different number
var float  lastSigEntry   = na
var float  lastSigStop    = na
var float  lastSigTp1     = na
var float  lastSigRunner  = na
var float  lastSigStopPts = na
var int    lastSigQty     = 0
var float  lastSigRisk    = na
var int    lastSigBar     = na
var string lastSigSess    = "-"
var string lastSigSwept   = "-"
var string lastSigTrig    = "-"
var int    lastSigBarLong  = na
var int    lastSigBarShort = na

// ---- Per-session signal counts, per direction -------------------------------
var int sigAsiaLong  = 0
var int sigAsiaShort = 0
var int sigLdnLong   = 0
var int sigLdnShort  = 0

// ---- Suppression counters. One per guard rail. ------------------------------
var int supSpent     = 0   // sweep already produced a trigger (primary debounce)
var int supInPos     = 0   // a virtual position is already open
var int supOutSess   = 0   // outside the signal-eligible session windows
var int supCutoff    = 0   // past the session no-new-entries cutoff
var int supExhaust   = 0   // session has already travelled too far
var int supMaxSess   = 0   // per-session, per-direction cap reached
var int supMinBars   = 0   // too close to the previous same-direction signal
var int supDecay     = 0   // score no longer passed on the trigger bar
var int supStopBand  = 0   // structural stop outside the min/max band
var int supAmbig     = 0   // both sides passed within the ambiguity margin
var int runnerFallbk = 0   // opposing pool unusable, fell back to fixed R

// Episode latches, so per-bar states are counted once rather than every bar.
var int  lastSpentCounted = na
var bool wasAmbiguous     = false

// ---- Per-bar visual outputs, reset every bar --------------------------------
float entryMarkLong  = na
float entryMarkShort = na

// ---- Signal line budget ------------------------------------------------------
var array<line> sigLines = array.new<line>()

f_pushSigLine(line l) =>
    array.push(sigLines, l)
    while array.size(sigLines) > MAX_SIG_LINES
        line.delete(array.shift(sigLines))

// ---- Alert message builders --------------------------------------------------
// alert(), NOT alertcondition(). alertcondition() does not fire through the
// "Any alert() function call" channel, which is the only practical way to route
// these to a phone. Messages are key=value pairs so they can be parsed
// downstream rather than only read.
f_sessName() =>
    string sname = inAsiaRaw ? "ASIA" : inLondonRaw ? "LONDON" : "OFF"
    sname

f_entryAlertMsg(bool isLong, float sc, float pk, float e, float st, float t1,
     float rn, float spts, string swept, int tier, string poiK, int qty,
     float riskAct, string trig) =>
    string m = alertPrefix + " | evt=ENTRY" +
             " | side=" + (isLong ? "LONG" : "SHORT") +
             " | score=" + str.tostring(sc, "#.00") +
             " | peak=" + str.tostring(pk, "#.00") +
             " | entry=" + str.tostring(e, format.mintick) +
             " | stop=" + str.tostring(st, format.mintick) +
             " | tp1=" + str.tostring(t1, format.mintick) +
             " | tp1pct=" + str.tostring(tp1Pct, "#") +
             " | runner=" + str.tostring(rn, format.mintick) +
             " | stopPts=" + str.tostring(spts, "#.00") +
             " | swept=" + swept +
             " | tier=" + str.tostring(tier) +
             " | poi=" + poiK +
             " | trigger=" + trig +
             " | session=" + f_sessName() +
             " | qty=" + str.tostring(qty) +
             " | risk=" + str.tostring(riskAct, "#.00")
    m

f_exitAlertMsg(string evt, bool isLong, float px, string extra) =>
    string m = alertPrefix + " | evt=" + evt +
             " | side=" + (isLong ? "LONG" : "SHORT") +
             " | price=" + str.tostring(px, format.mintick) +
             " | session=" + f_sessName() + extra
    m

if barstate.isconfirmed
    // =========================================================================
    // 1. SESSION BOOKKEEPING
    // =========================================================================
    if asiaOpenRaw
        sigAsiaLong  := 0
        sigAsiaShort := 0
    if londonOpenRaw
        sigLdnLong  := 0
        sigLdnShort := 0

    // Snapshot BEFORE exit management, so a stop-out and a fresh entry can
    // never land on the same bar.
    bool wasFlat = posDir == 0

    // =========================================================================
    // 2. MANAGE THE OPEN VIRTUAL POSITION
    // Stop is checked FIRST. On a bar that reaches both the stop and TP1 we
    // cannot know the order from bar data, and assuming the good fill first
    // would flatter every result.
    // =========================================================================
    if posDir != 0
        bool isL = posDir > 0
        bool hitStop = isL ? low <= posStop : high >= posStop
        bool hitTp1  = isL ? high >= posTp1 : low <= posTp1
        bool hitRun  = isL ? high >= posRunner : low <= posRunner

        if hitStop
            alert(f_exitAlertMsg(posTp1Hit ? "BREAKEVEN_STOP" : "STOP", isL, posStop,
                     " | qty=" + str.tostring(posQty)), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
            posDir := 0
        if not hitStop and hitTp1 and not posTp1Hit
            posTp1Hit := true
            alert(f_exitAlertMsg("TP1", isL, posTp1,
                     " | pct=" + str.tostring(tp1Pct, "#") +
                     " | qty=" + str.tostring(posQty)), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
            if moveToBeAfterTp1
                posStop := posEntry
        if not hitStop and hitRun
            alert(f_exitAlertMsg("RUNNER_TARGET", isL, posRunner,
                     " | qty=" + str.tostring(posQty)), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
            posDir := 0
        // Session flatten overrides everything still open.
        if posDir != 0 and flattenNow
            alert(f_exitAlertMsg("SESSION_FLATTEN", isL, close,
                     " | qty=" + str.tostring(posQty)), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
            posDir := 0

    // =========================================================================
    // 3. WHICH SIDE, IF ANY
    // Highest score wins. But two opposing setups scoring within the ambiguity
    // margin is the model being confused, not two opportunities: take neither.
    // =========================================================================
    bool  passL = scorePasses(true)
    bool  passS = scorePasses(false)
    float totL  = currentScore(true)
    float totS  = currentScore(false)

    bool ambiguous = passL and passS and math.abs(totL - totS) < ambiguityMargin
    if ambiguous and not wasAmbiguous
        supAmbig += 1
    wasAmbiguous := ambiguous

    int wantDir = 0
    if passL and not passS
        wantDir := 1
    if passS and not passL
        wantDir := -1
    if passL and passS and not ambiguous and totL > totS
        wantDir := 1
    if passL and passS and not ambiguous and totS > totL
        wantDir := -1

    // =========================================================================
    // 4. TRIGGER, THEN GUARD RAILS
    // =========================================================================
    if wantDir != 0
        bool  isLong = wantDir > 0
        Sweep sw     = getLiveSweep(not isLong)
        bool  ok     = not na(sw)

        // --- PRIMARY DEBOUNCE, evaluated first so a spent sweep cannot spam
        //     the trigger logic. Counted once per sweep, not once per bar.
        if ok and sw.spent
            if na(lastSpentCounted) or lastSpentCounted != sw.confirmBarIdx
                supSpent += 1
                lastSpentCounted := sw.confirmBarIdx
            ok := false

        // --- Resolve the trigger --------------------------------------------
        POI   p        = na
        bool  fire     = false
        float entryPx  = na
        string trigStr = "-"
        if ok
            p := bestPOI(isLong, close)

            // Retest: price trades back to the zone's CE and the bar still
            // closes on the correct side of its far edge. A bar that closes
            // beyond the far edge did not retest the zone, it broke it.
            bool trigRetest = false
            if not na(p) and isLong and low <= p.ce and close > p.bottom
                trigRetest := true
            if not na(p) and not isLong and high >= p.ce and close < p.top
                trigRetest := true

            bool mssBarNow = not na(lastStructBar) and lastStructBar == bar_index and lastStructType == "MSS" and ((isLong and lastStructDir > 0) or (not isLong and lastStructDir < 0))

            // The retest window is measured from the sweep's own MSS pairing,
            // which is the earliest bar the setup could have been armed.
            int  armBar     = sw.confirmBarIdx
            bool windowOpen = (bar_index - armBar) <= entryRetestBars + mssMaxBarsAfterSweep
            bool windowEnd  = (bar_index - armBar) == entryRetestBars + mssMaxBarsAfterSweep

            if entryMode == "MSS close" and mssBarNow
                fire    := true
                entryPx := close
                trigStr := "MSS_CLOSE"
            if entryMode == "Retest limit" and trigRetest and windowOpen
                fire    := true
                entryPx := p.ce
                trigStr := "RETEST"
            if entryMode == "Either" and trigRetest and windowOpen
                fire    := true
                entryPx := p.ce
                trigStr := "RETEST"
            // FALLBACK NOTE: "fall back to MSS close" cannot mean filling at the
            // MSS bar's price -- that price is several bars in the past and
            // claiming it would be look-back pricing. The honest fallback is a
            // market entry at the close of the bar the window expires on, and
            // the alert says MARKET_FALLBACK so it is never mistaken for a
            // retest fill.
            if entryMode == "Either" and not trigRetest and windowEnd
                fire    := true
                entryPx := close
                trigStr := "MARKET_FALLBACK"

            ok := fire

        // --- Guard rails. Each one counts only when it blocks a real trigger.
        if ok and not wasFlat
            supInPos += 1
            ok := false
        if ok and not (inAsiaSignal or inLondon)
            // inAsiaSignal is stage 1's signal-eligible Asia: it drops the
            // 00:00-02:00 tail when asiaExcludeLate is on.
            supOutSess += 1
            ok := false
        if ok and pastCutoff
            supCutoff += 1
            ok := false
        if ok
            float med = inAsiaRaw ? asiaMedRange : inLondonRaw ? londonMedRange : na
            if not na(med) and not na(curSessRange) and curSessRange > exhaustMult * med
                supExhaust += 1
                ok := false
        if ok
            int used = inAsiaRaw ? (isLong ? sigAsiaLong : sigAsiaShort) :
                       inLondonRaw ? (isLong ? sigLdnLong : sigLdnShort) : 0
            if used >= maxSignalsPerSession
                supMaxSess += 1
                ok := false
        if ok
            int lastBarSameDir = isLong ? lastSigBarLong : lastSigBarShort
            if not na(lastBarSameDir) and (bar_index - lastBarSameDir) < minBarsBetweenSameDir
                supMinBars += 1
                ok := false
        if ok and entryRequireScoreAtTrigger
            // Re-read the score on THIS bar. scLong/scShort were recomputed
            // earlier in this same confirmed pass, so this is the trigger-bar
            // score, not a stale one.
            if not scorePasses(isLong)
                supDecay += 1
                ok := false

        // --- Stop, and the suppression band ---------------------------------
        float buf     = f_stopBuffer()
        float stopPx  = na
        float stopPts = na
        if ok
            float stopSwept = isLong ? sw.sweepExtreme - buf : sw.sweepExtreme + buf
            float stopPoi   = na
            if not na(p)
                stopPoi := isLong ? p.bottom - buf : p.top + buf
            if stopMode == "Beyond swept extreme"
                stopPx := stopSwept
            if stopMode == "Beyond POI far edge"
                stopPx := na(stopPoi) ? stopSwept : stopPoi
            if stopMode == "Wider of the two"
                stopPx := na(stopPoi) ? stopSwept : (isLong ? math.min(stopSwept, stopPoi) : math.max(stopSwept, stopPoi))
            stopPts := isLong ? entryPx - stopPx : stopPx - entryPx
            // SUPPRESS, never clamp. A stop outside the band is the structure
            // saying it is not the structure we thought we had.
            if na(stopPts) or stopPts < stopMinPts or stopPts > stopMaxPts
                supStopBand += 1
                ok := false

        // --- Targets, sizing, and fire --------------------------------------
        if ok
            float tp1Px = isLong ? entryPx + tp1R * stopPts : entryPx - tp1R * stopPts

            Pool  opp     = isLong ? nearestBuySideAboveTier(entryPx, sweepMaxTier) : nearestSellSideBelowTier(entryPx, sweepMaxTier)
            // Built with an if, not a ternary: Pine evaluates both arms and
            // opp.price on an na object is a runtime error.
            float runPool = na
            if not na(opp)
                runPool := opp.price
            float runFix  = isLong ? entryPx + runnerFixedR * stopPts : entryPx - runnerFixedR * stopPts
            // A pool nearer than TP1 is not a runner target, it is an obstacle.
            bool poolUnusable = na(runPool)
            if not na(runPool) and isLong and runPool <= tp1Px
                poolUnusable := true
            if not na(runPool) and not isLong and runPool >= tp1Px
                poolUnusable := true

            float runnerPx = runFix
            if runnerTarget == "Next opposing pool" and not poolUnusable
                runnerPx := runPool
            if runnerTarget == "Either whichever first" and not poolUnusable
                runnerPx := isLong ? math.min(runPool, runFix) : math.max(runPool, runFix)
            if poolUnusable and runnerTarget != "Fixed R multiple"
                runnerFallbk += 1

            // Sizing. floor() then a floor of 1 contract, and we report the
            // ACTUAL dollar risk so the rounding error is visible rather than
            // implied.
            int   qty       = math.max(1, int(math.floor(riskUSD / (stopPts * MNQ_POINT_VALUE))))
            float riskAct   = qty * stopPts * MNQ_POINT_VALUE
            float peakNow   = isLong ? nz(peakLong, currentScore(true)) : nz(peakShort, currentScore(false))
            float scoreNow  = currentScore(isLong)

            // Burn the sweep. THE primary debounce.
            sw.spent := true

            posDir    := wantDir
            posEntry  := entryPx
            posStop   := stopPx
            posTp1    := tp1Px
            posRunner := runnerPx
            posTp1Hit := false
            posBar    := bar_index
            posQty    := qty

            lastSigDir     := wantDir
            lastSigScore   := scoreNow
            lastSigPeak    := peakNow
            lastSigEntry   := entryPx
            lastSigStop    := stopPx
            lastSigTp1     := tp1Px
            lastSigRunner  := runnerPx
            lastSigStopPts := stopPts
            lastSigQty     := qty
            lastSigRisk    := riskAct
            lastSigBar     := bar_index
            lastSigSess    := f_sessName()
            lastSigSwept   := sw.poolTag
            lastSigTrig    := trigStr
            if isLong
                lastSigBarLong := bar_index
            if not isLong
                lastSigBarShort := bar_index

            if inAsiaRaw and isLong
                sigAsiaLong += 1
            if inAsiaRaw and not isLong
                sigAsiaShort += 1
            if inLondonRaw and isLong
                sigLdnLong += 1
            if inLondonRaw and not isLong
                sigLdnShort += 1

            if isLong
                entryMarkLong := entryPx
            if not isLong
                entryMarkShort := entryPx

            string poiKindNow = "none"
            if not na(p)
                poiKindNow := p.kind
            alert(f_entryAlertMsg(isLong, scoreNow, peakNow, entryPx, stopPx, tp1Px,
                     runnerPx, stopPts, sw.poolTag, sw.poolTier, poiKindNow, qty,
                     riskAct, trigStr), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

            // --- Drawings: four short segments, not extended, so they cannot
            //     accumulate into a wall of lines across the chart.
            if showSignals
                color sc2 = isLong ? colSellSide : colBuySide
                f_pushSigLine(line.new(bar_index, entryPx, bar_index + 20, entryPx,
                         xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(sc2, 0), width = 2))
                f_pushSigLine(line.new(bar_index, stopPx, bar_index + 20, stopPx,
                         xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(color.red, 20),
                         style = line.style_dashed, width = 1))
                f_pushSigLine(line.new(bar_index, tp1Px, bar_index + 20, tp1Px,
                         xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(color.green, 20),
                         style = line.style_dotted, width = 1))
                f_pushSigLine(line.new(bar_index, runnerPx, bar_index + 20, runnerPx,
                         xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(color.green, 45),
                         style = line.style_dotted, width = 1))
                f_pushS2Label(label.new(bar_index, entryPx,
                         (isLong ? "LONG " : "SHORT ") + str.tostring(scoreNow, "#.00") +
                         "  x" + str.tostring(qty),
                         xloc = xloc.bar_index,
                         style = isLong ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down,
                         color = color.new(sc2, 75), textcolor = color.new(sc2, 0),
                         size = size.small))

// ---- Entry markers -----------------------------------------------------------
plotshape(showSignals ? entryMarkLong : na, title = "Long entry",
     style = shape.triangleup, location = location.absolute,
     color = color.new(colSellSide, 0), size = size.small)
plotshape(showSignals ? entryMarkShort : na, title = "Short entry",
     style = shape.triangledown, location = location.absolute,
     color = color.new(colBuySide, 0), size = size.small)

// =============================================================================
// SECTION E: DEBUG TABLE
// The stage-1 verification surface. Everything here is read from confirmed
// state, so if a number looks wrong the state is wrong, not the display.
// =============================================================================

f_px(float v) =>
    string s = na(v) ? "pending" : str.tostring(v, format.mintick)
    s

f_num(float v) =>
    string s = na(v) ? "n/a" : str.tostring(v, "#.##")
    s

// "price @ bar N" for a confirmed swing, or "pending".
f_swingStr(float px, int bidx) =>
    string s = "pending"
    if not na(px)
        s := str.tostring(px, format.mintick) + " @ " + str.tostring(bidx)
    s

// "price (tag)" for a pool, or "none".
f_poolStr(Pool p) =>
    string s = "none"
    if not na(p)
        s := str.tostring(p.price, format.mintick) + " (" + p.tag + ")"
    s

// "Asia High T0  7b left  MSS" for a live sweep, or "none".
f_liveSweepStr(Sweep sw) =>
    string s = "none"
    if not na(sw)
        s := sw.poolTag + "  T" + str.tostring(sw.poolTier) +
             "  " + str.tostring(sw.expiresAtBarIdx - bar_index) + "b left"
        if sw.mssConfirmed
            s := s + "  +MSS"
    s

// "MSS up  3b ago" for the last structure event, or "none".
f_structEvtStr(string kind, int dir, int bidx) =>
    string s = "none"
    if kind != "" and not na(bidx)
        s := kind + " " + (dir > 0 ? "up" : "down") + "  " + str.tostring(bar_index - bidx) + "b ago"
    s

// "12 swept / 5 broke  (2.4:1)  upg 3" -- the calibration ratio for
// breakoutClosesToInvalidate, plus how often a pending record was upgraded to
// a more significant pool. A high upgrade count means minor levels really were
// shadowing the ones that matter.
f_sweepRatioStr(int swept, int broke, int upg) =>
    string s = str.tostring(swept) + " swept / " + str.tostring(broke) + " broke"
    if broke > 0
        // *1.0 forces float division -- Pine truncates int/int, so 12/5 would
        // print 2 instead of 2.4 and the ratio would be useless.
        s := s + "  (" + str.tostring(swept * 1.0 / broke, "#.0") + ":1)"
    s := s + "  upg " + str.tostring(upg)
    s

// ---- stage-3 table helpers --------------------------------------------------
f_countFvgActive(bool bullish) =>
    int n = 0
    if array.size(fvgs) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(fvgs) - 1
            FVG g = array.get(fvgs, i)
            if g.state <= ST_CE_TAGGED and g.bullish == bullish
                n += 1
    n

f_countIfvgActive() =>
    int n = 0
    if array.size(ifvgs) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(ifvgs) - 1
            if array.get(ifvgs, i).state <= ST_CE_TAGGED
                n += 1
    n

f_countObState(bool breakers) =>
    int n = 0
    if array.size(obs) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(obs) - 1
            OB o = array.get(obs, i)
            if breakers and o.state == ST_BREAKER
                n += 1
            if not breakers and o.state <= ST_CE_TAGGED
                n += 1
    n

// "23150.25 - 23198.50  LONG" or "none".
f_drStr() =>
    string s = "none"
    if not na(drLow) and not na(drHigh)
        s := str.tostring(drLow, format.mintick) + " - " + str.tostring(drHigh, format.mintick)
        s := s + (drIsLong ? "  LONG" : "  SHORT")
    s

// "FVG @ 23172.75  q 0.85" or "none".
f_bestPoiStr(POI p) =>
    string s = "none"
    if not na(p)
        s := p.kind + " @ " + str.tostring(p.ce, format.mintick) + "  q " + str.tostring(p.quality, "#.00")
    s

// ---- stage-5 table helpers --------------------------------------------------
// "2.40 / 3.00" -- earned against the component's own maximum.
f_cmp(float earned, float maxv) =>
    string s = str.tostring(earned, "#.00") + " / " + str.tostring(maxv, "#.00")
    s

f_bucketTotal() =>
    int n = 0
    if array.size(scoreBuckets) == 5
        for i = 0 to 4
            n += array.get(scoreBuckets, i)
    n

// "  (93%)" or "" when the denominator is zero.
f_pctStr(int num, int den) =>
    string r = ""
    if den > 0
        r := "  (" + str.tostring(num * 100.0 / den, "#") + "%)"
    r

// Every bucket carries its own edge, so the row reads as a histogram even when
// it is all zeros. The previous bare "0 / 0 / 0 / 0 / 0" was indistinguishable
// from an empty row, which is how it got missed.
f_bucketStr() =>
    string s = ""
    if array.size(scoreBuckets) == 5
        s := "<5 "    + str.tostring(array.get(scoreBuckets, 0)) +
             " | 5-6 " + str.tostring(array.get(scoreBuckets, 1)) +
             " | 6-7 " + str.tostring(array.get(scoreBuckets, 2)) +
             " | 7-8 " + str.tostring(array.get(scoreBuckets, 3)) +
             " | 8+ "  + str.tostring(array.get(scoreBuckets, 4)) +
             "   (total " + str.tostring(f_bucketTotal()) + ")"
    s

// ---- stage-6 table helpers --------------------------------------------------
f_sigSideStr() =>
    string r = "none"
    if lastSigDir > 0
        r := "LONG"
    if lastSigDir < 0
        r := "SHORT"
    r

f_posStr() =>
    string r = "flat"
    if posDir > 0
        r := "LONG open"
    if posDir < 0
        r := "SHORT open"
    if posDir != 0 and posTp1Hit
        r := r + ", TP1 taken"
    r

var table dbg = na

if barstate.islast and showDebugTable
    if na(dbg)
        // Sized for the full table; compact mode simply leaves the rest empty.
        dbg := table.new(position.top_right, 2, 58,
             border_width = 1, border_color = color.new(color.gray, 60),
             frame_width  = 1, frame_color  = color.new(color.gray, 40))

    // Cells persist until overwritten, so clear before filling. That is what
    // lets the two modes share one table object without stale rows from the
    // other mode bleeding through.
    table.clear(dbg, 0, 0, 1, 57)

    // =========================================================================
    // COMPACT MODE. Only what is needed to judge whether the model is
    // discriminating. The histogram is at ROW 3 so it can never be the row that
    // scrolls off the bottom.
    // =========================================================================
    if compactTable
        color kHdr = color.new(color.blue, 80)
        color kBg  = color.new(color.black, 80)
        color kTx  = color.new(color.white, 0)

        string kSess = not inAnySession ? "NONE" : inAsia ? "ASIA" : "LONDON"
        string kArmL = "-"
        string kArmS = "-"
        if not na(scLong) and scLong.gateOk
            kArmL := str.tostring(scLong.total, "#.00") + (scLong.pass ? " PASS" : "")
        if not na(scShort) and scShort.gateOk
            kArmS := str.tostring(scShort.total, "#.00") + (scShort.pass ? " PASS" : "")
        string kSig = "none"
        if lastSigDir != 0
            kSig := (lastSigDir > 0 ? "LONG " : "SHORT ") + str.tostring(lastSigScore, "#.00") +
                     "  e " + str.tostring(lastSigEntry, format.mintick) +
                     "  x" + str.tostring(lastSigQty)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 0, "MNQ ICT  DIAG", bgcolor = kHdr, text_color = kTx, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 0, "counts are act | cum", bgcolor = kHdr, text_color = kTx, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 1, "Day / session", bgcolor = kBg, text_color = kTx, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 1, str.tostring(tradingDay) + "  " + tradingDateStr + "  " + kSess, bgcolor = kBg, text_color = kTx, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 2, "Sweep : breakout", bgcolor = kBg, text_color = kTx, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 2, f_sweepRatioStr(sweepConfirmedCount, breakoutRejectedCount, sweepUpgradeCount), bgcolor = kBg, text_color = kTx, text_size = size.small)

        // THE diagnostic. Clustering in one bucket means the model is not
        // discriminating, whatever the other rows say.
        // THE diagnostic, directly under Sweep:breakout so it is never the row
        // that scrolls off. Clustering in one bucket means the model is not
        // discriminating, whatever every other row says.
        table.cell(dbg, 0, 3, "Scores", bgcolor = kHdr, text_color = kTx, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 3, f_bucketStr(), bgcolor = kHdr, text_color = kTx, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 4, "Sup: debounce", bgcolor = kBg, text_color = kTx, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 4, "spent " + str.tostring(supSpent) +
                 " | inpos " + str.tostring(supInPos) +
                 " | bars " + str.tostring(supMinBars) +
                 " | max " + str.tostring(supMaxSess) +
                 " | ambig " + str.tostring(supAmbig), bgcolor = kBg, text_color = kTx, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 5, "Sup: context", bgcolor = kBg, text_color = kTx, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 5, "sess " + str.tostring(supOutSess) +
                 " | cut " + str.tostring(supCutoff) +
                 " | exh " + str.tostring(supExhaust) +
                 " | stop " + str.tostring(supStopBand) +
                 " | decay " + str.tostring(supDecay) +
                 " | runFB " + str.tostring(runnerFallbk), bgcolor = kBg, text_color = kTx, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 6, "Last signal", bgcolor = kBg, text_color = kTx, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 6, kSig, bgcolor = kBg, text_color = kTx, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 7, "Armed L | S", bgcolor = kBg, text_color = kTx, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 7, kArmL + "   |   " + kArmS, bgcolor = kBg, text_color = kTx, text_size = size.small)

        // Temporary, for the SMT pool-gate investigation.
        table.cell(dbg, 0, 8, "SMT cand|pass, dist", bgcolor = kBg, text_color = kTx, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 8, str.tostring(smtCandidates) + " | " + str.tostring(smtCount) +
                 "   d " + f_num(smtLastDistAny) + " / " + f_num(smtLastDistSig) + " / " + f_num(smtLastDistProt) + "t", bgcolor = kBg, text_color = kTx, text_size = size.small)

    if not compactTable
        color hdrBg  = color.new(color.blue, 80)
        color cellBg = color.new(color.black, 80)
        color txt    = color.new(color.white, 0)

        string sessName = not inAnySession ? "NONE" :
                          inAsia ? (inAsiaSignal ? "ASIA" : "ASIA (late, muted)") : "LONDON"
        int    sessBars = inAsiaRaw ? asiaBars : inLondonRaw ? londonBars : 0
        string closedStr = asiaJustClosed ? "ASIA closed" : londonJustClosed ? "LONDON closed" : "-"

        Pool nBuy  = nearestBuySideAbove(close)
        Pool nSell = nearestSellSideBelow(close)

        // Tier breakdown + saturation. If T2 is pinned and the total sits at the
        // cap, the book is under eviction pressure.
        // Tier breakdown, saturation, and how many are still ACTIVE. Stage 2
        // consumes pools on sweeps and breakouts, so act < total is now normal and
        // a large gap means most of the book has already been taken out.
        string tierStr = "T0 " + str.tostring(f_tierCount(TIER_PROTECTED)) +
                         " | T1 " + str.tostring(f_tierCount(TIER_SIGNIFICANT)) +
                         " | T2 " + str.tostring(f_tierCount(TIER_TRANSIENT)) +
                         "  (" + str.tostring(array.size(pools)) + "/" + str.tostring(maxPools) + ")" +
                         "  act " + str.tostring(activePoolCount())

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 0, "MNQ ICT  COMPLETE", bgcolor = hdrBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 0, "confirmed bars only", bgcolor = hdrBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 1, "Trading day", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 1, str.tostring(tradingDay) + "  " + tradingDateStr, bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 2, "Session", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 2, sessName, bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 3, "Bars into", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 3, str.tostring(sessBars), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 4, "Just closed", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 4, closedStr, bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 5, "Sess range", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 5, f_num(curSessRange), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 6, "Median 20", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 6, f_num(curSessMed) + "  (A " + f_num(asiaMedRange) + " / L " + f_num(londonMedRange) + ")", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 7, "ATR " + str.tostring(atrLen), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 7, f_num(atr), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 8, "Asia High", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 8, f_px(asiaRangeHigh), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 9, "Asia Low", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 9, f_px(asiaRangeLow), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 10, "PDH", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 10, f_px(pdh), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 11, "PDL", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 11, f_px(pdl), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 12, "PWH", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 12, f_px(pwh), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 13, "PWL", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 13, f_px(pwl), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 14, "Pools by tier", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 14, tierStr, bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 15, "Last swing H", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 15, f_swingStr(lastConfirmedSwingHigh, lastSwingHighBar), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 16, "Last swing L", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 16, f_swingStr(lastConfirmedSwingLow, lastSwingLowBar), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 17, "Nearest pool", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 17, "up " + f_poolStr(nBuy) + " | dn " + f_poolStr(nSell), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        // ---- STAGE 2 ROWS --------------------------------------------------------
        string biasStr = structBias > 0 ? "BULL" : structBias < 0 ? "BEAR" : "NEUTRAL"
        string dispStr = isDisplacementUp ? "UP" : isDisplacementDown ? "DOWN" : "none"
        bool   longArmed  = isSweepMssPair(false)   // sell-side swept, bullish MSS
        bool   shortArmed = isSweepMssPair(true)    // buy-side swept, bearish MSS
        string armedStr = longArmed and shortArmed ? "BOTH (?)" :
                          longArmed ? "LONG" : shortArmed ? "SHORT" : "none"

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 18, "S2 bias", bgcolor = hdrBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 18, biasStr, bgcolor = hdrBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 19, "Displacement", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 19, dispStr, bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 20, "Live sweep BUY", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 20, f_liveSweepStr(getLiveSweep(true)), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 21, "Live sweep SELL", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 21, f_liveSweepStr(getLiveSweep(false)), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 22, "Last structure", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 22, f_structEvtStr(lastStructType, lastStructDir, lastStructBar), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 23, "Sweep+MSS armed", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 23, armedStr, bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 24, "Sweep : breakout", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 24, f_sweepRatioStr(sweepConfirmedCount, breakoutRejectedCount, sweepUpgradeCount), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        // ---- STAGE 3 ROWS --------------------------------------------------------
        POI poiLong  = bestPOI(true,  close)
        POI poiShort = bestPOI(false, close)
        string oteNowStr = inOTE(true) ? "LONG" : inOTE(false) ? "SHORT" : "no"
        if not hasDealingRange()
            oteNowStr := "no range"

        // ZONE COUNTS: "active | cum". Active alone is ambiguous -- 0 could be a
        // quiet moment or could mean the zone type essentially never forms, and
        // those demand opposite responses.
        table.cell(dbg, 0, 25, "S3 zones  act | cum", bgcolor = hdrBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 25, "FVG b/s  " + str.tostring(f_countFvgActive(true)) + " / " + str.tostring(f_countFvgActive(false)) +
                 "  |  cum " + str.tostring(cumFvgBull) + " / " + str.tostring(cumFvgBear), bgcolor = hdrBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 26, "IFVG", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 26, str.tostring(f_countIfvgActive()) + "  |  cum " + str.tostring(cumIfvg), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 27, "OB / breaker", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 27, str.tostring(f_countObState(false)) + " / " + str.tostring(f_countObState(true)) +
                 "  |  cum " + str.tostring(cumOb) + " / " + str.tostring(cumBreaker), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 28, "Dealing range", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 28, f_drStr(), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 29, "In OTE now", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 29, oteNowStr, bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 30, "bestPOI long", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 30, f_bestPoiStr(poiLong), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 31, "bestPOI short", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 31, f_bestPoiStr(poiShort), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 32, "FVG+OB overlap", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 32, str.tostring(fvgObCoincidenceCount), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        // ---- STAGE 4 ROWS --------------------------------------------------------
        string smtStateStr = "none"
        if smtDivergence(true)
            smtStateStr := "BULLISH  " + str.tostring(smtStrengthNow(), "#.00")
        if smtDivergence(false)
            smtStateStr := "BEARISH  " + str.tostring(smtStrengthNow(), "#.00")
        if not smtEnabled
            smtStateStr := "disabled"

        // If this reads "no feed" the reference is not delivering and every SMT
        // result below is silently absent rather than wrong.
        string refFeedStr = na(refClose) ? "no feed" : str.tostring(refClose, format.mintick)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 33, "S4 SMT", bgcolor = hdrBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 33, smtStateStr, bgcolor = hdrBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 34, "Ref feed", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 34, smtSymbol + "  " + refFeedStr, bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 35, "SMT cand | passed", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 35, str.tostring(smtCandidates) + "  |  " + str.tostring(smtCount), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        // ---- STAGE 5 ROWS --------------------------------------------------------
        // Show whichever side is armed. If both are, show the higher-scoring one.
        Score shown = na
        bool  gL = not na(scLong)  and scLong.gateOk
        bool  gS = not na(scShort) and scShort.gateOk
        if gL and not gS
            shown := scLong
        if gS and not gL
            shown := scShort
        if gL and gS and scLong.total >= scShort.total
            shown := scLong
        if gL and gS and scShort.total > scLong.total
            shown := scShort

        string armedStr2 = "none"
        string sweepStr  = "-"
        string mssStr    = "-"
        string poiStr2   = "-"
        string locStr    = "-"
        string smtPtsStr = "-"
        string sessStr   = "-"
        string totalStr  = "-"
        string verdict   = "-"
        if not na(shown)
            armedStr2 := shown.isLong ? "LONG" : "SHORT"
            sweepStr  := f_cmp(shown.sweepPts, wSweep) + "  (" + shown.poolTag + " T" + str.tostring(shown.poolTier) + ")"
            mssStr    := f_cmp(shown.mssPts, wMss)
            poiStr2   := f_cmp(shown.poiPts, wPoi) + "  (" + shown.poiKind + ")"
            locStr    := f_cmp(shown.locPts, wLocation)
            smtPtsStr := f_cmp(shown.smtPts, wSmt) + (inAsia ? "  asia x0.5" : "")
            sessStr   := f_cmp(shown.sessPts, wSessionPd)
            totalStr  := str.tostring(shown.total, "#.00") + "  vs " + str.tostring(scoreThreshold, "#.0")
            verdict   := shown.strong ? "PASS - STRONG" : shown.pass ? "PASS - signal" : "FAIL"

        // Built with explicit ifs, not a ternary chain: Pine evaluates both arms of
        // a ternary, and shown.strong on an na object is a runtime error.
        color vBg = cellBg
        if not na(shown) and shown.strong
            vBg := color.new(color.green, 55)
        if not na(shown) and shown.pass and not shown.strong
            vBg := color.new(color.green, 75)
        if not na(shown) and not shown.pass
            vBg := color.new(color.red, 78)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 36, "S5 armed", bgcolor = hdrBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 36, armedStr2, bgcolor = hdrBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 37, "Sweep", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 37, sweepStr, bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 38, "MSS", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 38, mssStr, bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 39, "POI", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 39, poiStr2, bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 40, "DR location", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 40, locStr, bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 41, "SMT", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 41, smtPtsStr, bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 42, "Session P/D", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 42, sessStr, bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 43, "TOTAL", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 43, totalStr, bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 44, "Verdict", bgcolor = vBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 44, verdict, bgcolor = vBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        // THE diagnostic. One sample per armed setup, at its peak score. Clustering
        // in a single bucket means the model is not discriminating.
        table.cell(dbg, 0, 45, "Score distribution", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 45, f_bucketStr(), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        // ---- STAGE 6 ROWS --------------------------------------------------------
        string sigHdr = "none"
        string sigLv1 = "-"
        string sigLv2 = "-"
        string sigLv3 = "-"
        if lastSigDir != 0
            sigHdr := f_sigSideStr() + "  " + str.tostring(lastSigScore, "#.00") +
                      "  (peak " + str.tostring(lastSigPeak, "#.00") + ")"
            sigLv1 := "e " + str.tostring(lastSigEntry, format.mintick) +
                      "  s " + str.tostring(lastSigStop, format.mintick) +
                      "  (" + str.tostring(lastSigStopPts, "#.0") + "pt)"
            sigLv2 := "t1 " + str.tostring(lastSigTp1, format.mintick) +
                      "  run " + str.tostring(lastSigRunner, format.mintick)
            sigLv3 := "x" + str.tostring(lastSigQty) + "  $" + str.tostring(lastSigRisk, "#.00") +
                      "  " + lastSigSess + "  " + lastSigTrig

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 46, "S6 last signal", bgcolor = hdrBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 46, sigHdr, bgcolor = hdrBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 47, "Entry / stop", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 47, sigLv1, bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 48, "TP1 / runner", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 48, sigLv2, bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 49, "Size / risk", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 49, sigLv3, bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 50, "Swept / position", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 50, lastSigSwept + "  |  " + f_posStr(), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 51, "Session signals", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 51, "Asia L" + str.tostring(sigAsiaLong) + " S" + str.tostring(sigAsiaShort) +
                 "  |  Ldn L" + str.tostring(sigLdnLong) + " S" + str.tostring(sigLdnShort) +
                 "  (max " + str.tostring(maxSignalsPerSession) + ")", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        // Which guard rail is actually doing the work. Each counts blocked
        // TRIGGERS, not bars, so these are comparable to each other.
        table.cell(dbg, 0, 52, "Sup: debounce", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 52, "spent " + str.tostring(supSpent) +
                 " | inpos " + str.tostring(supInPos) +
                 " | bars " + str.tostring(supMinBars) +
                 " | max " + str.tostring(supMaxSess) +
                 " | ambig " + str.tostring(supAmbig), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 53, "Sup: context", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 53, "sess " + str.tostring(supOutSess) +
                 " | cut " + str.tostring(supCutoff) +
                 " | exh " + str.tostring(supExhaust) +
                 " | stop " + str.tostring(supStopBand) +
                 " | decay " + str.tostring(supDecay) +
                 " | runFB " + str.tostring(runnerFallbk), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        // ---- TEMPORARY INVESTIGATION ROWS ----------------------------------------
        table.cell(dbg, 0, 54, "SMT pool dist", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 54, "any " + f_num(smtLastDistAny) + "  |  T0-1 " + f_num(smtLastDistSig) + "  |  T0 " + f_num(smtLastDistProt) + "  ticks", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

        table.cell(dbg, 0, 55, "Armed w/ DR", bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(dbg, 1, 55, str.tostring(armedWithDR) + " / " + str.tostring(armedSetups) + f_pctStr(armedWithDR, armedSetups), bgcolor = cellBg, text_color = txt, text_size = size.small)

// Remove the table if the user switches it off mid-session.
if barstate.islast and not showDebugTable and not na(dbg)
    table.delete(dbg)
    dbg := na

// =============================================================================
// SECTION F: STAGE STUBS
// Nothing below this line is implemented yet. The order is fixed; each stage
// fills in its own block and touches nothing else.
// =============================================================================

// ===== STAGE 2: DISPLACEMENT / SWEEP DETECTION ===== IMPLEMENTED
// Lives above the debug table, as sections G / H / I / J, because the table
// consumes its output and Pine requires declaration before use.
// Stage-2 API now available to later stages:
//   isDisplacementUp / isDisplacementDown
//   getLiveSweep(buySide) -> Sweep, isSweepMssPair(buySide) -> bool
//   structBias, lastStructType / lastStructDir / lastStructBar
//   lastBreakoutDir, sweepConfirmedCount, breakoutRejectedCount

// ===== STAGE 3: FVG / IFVG / ORDER BLOCKS / OTE ===== IMPLEMENTED
// Lives above the debug table, as sections K / L / M / N / O / P.
// Stage-3 API now available to later stages:
//   bestPOI(isLong, px) -> POI     THE single query. One component, not two.
//   poiBook (array<POI>), rebuilt on every confirmed bar
//   hasDealingRange(), inDiscount(), inPremium(), inOTE(isLong)
//   drLow / drHigh / drEq / drIsLong, na when no range is defined
//   fvgs / ifvgs / obs arrays and the ST_* state enum
//   fvgObCoincidenceCount

// ===== STAGE 4: SMT DIVERGENCE (MNQ vs ES) ===== IMPLEMENTED
// Lives above the debug table, as section Q.
// Stage-4 API now available to later stages:
//   smtDivergence(bullish) -> bool
//   smtStrengthNow()       -> float 0-1   (graded; see the note at the function)
//   smtCount, refHigh / refLow / refClose (na when the reference has no data)
// SMT is confluence only. It never arms a setup and never writes to sweep,
// structure or POI state.

// ===== STAGE 5: CONFLUENCE SCORING ===== IMPLEMENTED
// Lives above the debug table, as section R.
// Stage-5 API now available to stage 6:
//   scoreFor(isLong)     -> Score   full breakdown, never just a number
//   currentScore(isLong) -> float
//   scorePasses(isLong)  -> bool
//   scoreBuckets (array<int>, 5)  peak score per armed setup
// The mandatory gate lives inside f_computeScore: no sweep with a paired MSS
// means every component is zero, so peripheral evidence can never arm a setup.

// ===== STAGE 6: ENTRY TRIGGER, GUARD RAILS, ALERTS ===== IMPLEMENTED
// Lives above the debug table, as section S. All six stages are now complete.
//
// ALERT SETUP: create ONE alert on this indicator with the condition set to
// "Any alert() function call". alertcondition() is deliberately not used
// anywhere in this script, because alertcondition alerts do not fire through
// that channel and cannot carry a computed message.
//
// Alert events, all key=value parseable:
//   ENTRY | TP1 | STOP | BREAKEVEN_STOP | RUNNER_TARGET | SESSION_FLATTEN
